window.GEAR_BOOK_CONTENTS["book-23"] = [{"id":1,"rawContent":"# 第 17 章　回到那一天\n\n靜止的操場上，陽光一動也不動。\n\n五十二個孩子站在那裡，像闖進了一幅畫。\n\n「現在呢？」阿達問。他的聲音，在空曠的操場上迴盪。\n\n「他看不到我們。」晴晴指著畫面裡的小林澈。\n\n小小的林澈站在隊伍最後面，半舉著手，眼睛盯著地面。\n\n「是嗎？」林澈忽然說。\n\n他蹲下來，正對著小林澈。\n\n「嘿。」他輕輕喊。\n\n小林澈的肩膀，動了一下。\n\n他慢慢地、慢慢地，抬起頭。\n\n他的眼睛，直直地看著林澈。\n\n看到了。\n\n孩子們全都倒抽一口氣。\n\n「他……看得到你！」B 晴晴低聲說。\n\n「只有林澈，看得到林澈。」小筠說，「因為這是『林澈的那天』。」\n\n小林澈瞪大眼睛，嘴巴張得圓圓的。\n\n他看看 A 林澈，又看看 B 林澈。\n\n「你們……」他的聲音小得幾乎聽不見，「你們是誰？」\n\n他聽得到！\n\n「我們是……」A 林澈張了張嘴，一時不知道怎麼說。\n\n「我們是你。」B 林澈說。\n\n小林澈愣住了。\n\n「我是你，如果那一天，你舉了手，然後老師說『你可以』。」B 林澈說。\n\n「我也是你。」A 林澈說，「我舉了手。可是，老師讓我退了下來。」\n\n小林澈低下頭，看著自己舉到一半的手。\n\n「所以……」他小聲說，「這隻手，最後還是放下了嗎？」\n\nA 林澈沒有回答。\n\n「放下了。」B 林澈說，「可是，那不代表你不勇敢。」\n\n小林澈抬起頭，眼睛裡霧霧的。\n\n就在這時，畫面動了。\n\n劉老師走了過來。一步，兩步。\n\n「時間又開始了！」阿達大喊。\n\n劉老師張開嘴——\n\n啪。\n\n世界，重置了。\n\n陽光還是一樣。隊伍還是一樣。小林澈的手，又舉回了半空中。\n\n劉老師，又站在隊伍前面。好像剛才的一切，都沒有發生過。\n\n「這是……」晴晴瞪大眼睛，「循環？」\n\n「這一天，一直在重複。」小筠喃喃，「因為那天有兩種可能。世界選不出來，所以，一直在重播。」\n\n「那怎麼辦？」阿達抓頭。\n\n孩子們開始想辦法。\n\n小陽衝到劉老師面前，大吼：「老師！選『你可以』！」\n\n劉老師沒有任何反應。\n\n阿達撿起一顆石頭，丟向畫面裡的接力棒——石頭穿了過去，滾到一邊。\n\n晴晴把筆記本翻開，對著劉老師大聲念規則——當然，也沒用。\n\n「沒用的。」B 林澈搖頭，「這裡的一切，都是記憶。我們改變不了。」\n\n「那我們到底來這裡做什麼？」小陽洩氣地坐下來。\n\n孩子們安靜了。\n\n林澈看著那個小小的自己。\n\n小小的他，又一次舉起半隻手，又一次猶豫。\n\n「也許，我們不是來改變的。」林澈輕聲說。\n\n「我們是來『看』的。」他轉過頭，「也讓他看到。」\n\n「看到什麼？」阿達問。\n\n「看到兩種可能，都是真的。」林澈說，「看到不管選哪一條路，他都會長大，都會被愛，都會……好好的。」\n\n風，好像動了一下。\n\n雖然這裡的風，是記憶裡的風，可是孩子們都感覺到了。\n\n「我們要怎麼讓他看到？」B 晴晴問。\n\n小筠想了想：「兩個林澈，各講一半。講你們的人生。一個講『放下手之後』，一個講『跑出去之後』。」\n\n「讓他看見，兩條路，都走得通。」她說。\n\n兩個林澈對看一眼。\n\n然後，他們一起，走到小林澈面前。\n\n小林澈抬頭看著他們。他的眼睛，像兩口小小的井。\n\nB 林澈先開口。\n\n「我跑了最後一棒。」他說，「全班在叫我的名字。風很大，我衝過終點線。從那天起，我變成班上最閃亮的人。」\n\n「可是，」他停了一下，「我也會累。大家都依賴我，我不能停下來。我很怕有一天，自己跑不動了。」\n\n小林澈安靜地聽著。\n\nA 林澈接著說。\n\n「我沒有跑。」他說，「我退到了最後面。我變得很安靜，安靜到像影子一樣。」\n\n「可是，」他深吸一口氣，「我也學會了看。我看見別人看不見的小事。我發現了舊禮堂的鏡子。我認識了晴晴、阿達、小筠、安安。」\n\n「然後，我走到了你面前。」\n\n小林澈的眼睛，亮了一點點。\n\n「所以，」兩個林澈同時說——\n\n「兩條路，都很好。」\n\n操場上，安靜得只剩下記憶裡的蟬聲。\n\n小林澈看著自己的手。\n\n那隻舉到一半的手，還停在半空中。\n\n「可是……」他的聲音小小的，「我不知道，要舉，還是要放。」\n\n「你不用現在知道。」A 林澈說。\n\n「那一天的你，只要做當時的你，就夠了。」B 林澈說。\n\n小林澈慢慢地、慢慢地，把頭抬起來。\n\n他的眼睛，第一次，直直地看向兩個林澈。\n\n「那我……可以抱抱你們嗎？」\n\n兩個林澈愣住了。\n\n然後，他們同時蹲下來，張開雙臂。\n\n小林澈撲了過去。\n\n三個林澈，抱在一起。\n\n就在那一瞬間——\n\n銀白色的光，從他們三個人中間，綻放開來。\n\n光，像漣漪一樣擴散，掃過整個操場。\n\n記憶裡的世界，開始變亮。亮得刺眼。\n\n孩子們不由自主地閉上眼睛。\n\n等他們再張開眼睛的時候——\n\n他們已經回到了舊禮堂。\n\n鏡子，還在。可是鏡面上的裂紋，變小了。\n\n只有一點點。可是，真的變小了。\n\n「你們看！」阿達衝到鏡子前。\n\n裂紋正在慢慢地、慢慢地，往中間合攏。\n\n像一道正在癒合的傷口。\n\n「成功了！」小陽跳起來。\n\n「還沒有。」小筠說。\n\n她指著鏡子。裂紋合到一半，停住了。\n\n鏡面裡，那個靜止的操場，還在。小林澈的手，還是舉在半空中。\n\n「還差最後一步。」小筠說，「而且那一步，不在鏡子裡。」\n\n「在哪裡？」晴晴問。\n\n小筠轉過頭，看著兩個林澈。\n\n「在你們自己身上。」\n\n操場上——不，禮堂裡，安靜了下來。\n\n晴晴低頭看手錶。\n\n「十一點二十分。」\n\n兩個林澈，隔著一步的距離，看著對方。\n\n他們都知道，小筠說得對。\n\n那一句還沒說出口的話，那一個還沒放下的東西——\n\n在他們兩個的心裡。\n\n「接下來，」B 林澈說，聲音很輕，「該輪到我們了。」\n\n林澈點頭。\n\n兩個長得一模一樣的少年，同時把手，放在自己的心口上。\n\n「我們之間，還有一面鏡子。」B 林澈說。\n\n「今晚，我們把它打碎。」林澈說。\n\n海風從舊禮堂的門縫鑽進來，吹得鏡面微微發亮。\n\n十一點二十分。\n\n真正的決戰，現在才開始。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 17 — Back to That Day\n\nOn the frozen playground, the sunlight didn't move at all.\n\nThe fifty-two children stood there, as if they'd stumbled into a painting.\n\n\"What now?\" A-Da asked. His voice echoed across the empty playground.\n\n\"He can't see us,\" Ching-Ching pointed at little Lin Che in the scene.\n\nLittle Lin Che stood at the back of the line, hand half-raised, eyes on the ground.\n\n\"Can't he?\" Lin Che suddenly said.\n\nHe crouched down, facing little Lin Che directly.\n\n\"Hey,\" he called softly.\n\nLittle Lin Che's shoulders twitched.\n\nHe slowly, slowly lifted his head.\n\nHis eyes looked straight at Lin Che.\n\nHe could see.\n\nAll the children gasped.\n\n\"He... he can see you!\" B Ching-Ching whispered.\n\n\"Only Lin Che can see Lin Che,\" Hsiao-Yun said. \"Because this is 'Lin Che's day.'\"\n\nLittle Lin Che's eyes went wide, his mouth a perfect circle.\n\nHe looked from A Lin Che to B Lin Che.\n\n\"You...\" his voice was so small it was barely audible. \"Who are you?\"\n\nHe could hear them!\n\n\"We are...\" A Lin Che opened his mouth, not knowing how to say it.\n\n\"We are you,\" B Lin Che said.\n\nLittle Lin Che froze.\n\n\"I'm you, if that day you raised your hand, and the teacher said 'you can do it,'\" B Lin Che said.\n\n\"I'm you too,\" A Lin Che said. \"I raised my hand. But the teacher had me step back.\"\n\nLittle Lin Che lowered his head and looked at his half-raised hand.\n\n\"So...\" he said quietly. \"This hand ended up going down after all, didn't it?\"\n\nA Lin Che didn't answer.\n\n\"It did go down,\" B Lin Che said. \"But that doesn't mean you weren't brave.\"\n\nLittle Lin Che looked up, his eyes misty.\n\nJust then, the scene moved.\n\nCoach Liu walked over. One step, two steps.\n\n\"Time is moving again!\" A-Da shouted.\n\nCoach Liu opened his mouth—\n\nPop.\n\nThe world reset.\n\nThe sunshine was the same. The line was the same. Little Lin Che's hand had risen back to halfway.\n\nCoach Liu stood at the front of the line again, as if none of what just happened had ever happened.\n\n\"This is...\" Ching-Ching's eyes went wide. \"A loop?\"\n\n\"This day keeps repeating,\" Hsiao-Yun murmured. \"Because that day has two possibilities. The world can't choose, so it keeps replaying.\"\n\n\"Then what do we do?\" A-Da scratched his head.\n\nThe children began brainstorming solutions.\n\nXiao-Yang dashed up to Coach Liu and yelled: \"Teacher! Pick 'you can do it'!\"\n\nCoach Liu didn't react at all.\n\nA-Da picked up a stone and threw it at the baton in the scene — the stone passed through and rolled away.\n\nChing-Ching flipped open her notebook and read the rules out loud at Coach Liu — of course, that didn't work either.\n\n\"It's no use.\" B Lin Che shook his head. \"Everything here is memory. We can't change it.\"\n\n\"Then what did we even come here for?\" Xiao-Yang sat down in defeat.\n\nThe children fell quiet.\n\nLin Che looked at the little version of himself.\n\nLittle him raised his hand halfway once again, hesitating once again.\n\n\"Maybe we didn't come here to change anything,\" Lin Che said softly.\n\n\"We came here to 'see.'\" He turned around. \"And to let him see too.\"\n\n\"See what?\" A-Da asked.\n\n\"To see that both possibilities are real,\" Lin Che said. \"To see that whichever path he takes, he'll grow up, he'll be loved, he'll be... okay.\"\n\nThe wind seemed to stir.\n\nEven though this wind was a memory's wind, all the children felt it.\n\n\"How do we let him see?\" B Ching-Ching asked.\n\nHsiao-Yun thought for a moment: \"Two Lin Ches, each tell half. Tell him about your lives. One tells 'after the hand went down,' the other tells 'after running out.'\"\n\n\"Let him see that both paths go somewhere,\" she said.\n\nThe two Lin Ches exchanged a glance.\n\nThen, together, they walked up to little Lin Che.\n\nLittle Lin Che looked up at them. His eyes were like two tiny wells.\n\nB Lin Che spoke first.\n\n\"I ran the anchor leg,\" he said. \"The whole class was shouting my name. The wind was strong, and I sprinted across the finish line. From that day on, I became the brightest person in my class.\"\n\n\"But,\" he paused, \"I get tired too. Everyone depends on me. I can't stop. I'm afraid that one day, I won't be able to run anymore.\"\n\nLittle Lin Che listened quietly.\n\nA Lin Che spoke next.\n\n\"I didn't run,\" he said. \"I retreated to the very back. I became very quiet, quiet as a shadow.\"\n\n\"But,\" he took a deep breath, \"I also learned how to watch. I saw small things others couldn't see. I found the mirror in the old auditorium. I met Ching-Ching, A-Da, Hsiao-Yun, and An-An.\"\n\n\"Then, I walked all the way here, to you.\"\n\nLittle Lin Che's eyes brightened a little.\n\n\"So,\" the two Lin Ches said at the same time—\n\n\"Both paths are good.\"\n\nThe playground went so silent that only the memory's cicadas could be heard.\n\nLittle Lin Che looked at his own hand.\n\nThe half-raised hand still hung in the air.\n\n\"But...\" his voice was tiny. \"I don't know whether to raise it, or let it go.\"\n\n\"You don't have to know right now,\" A Lin Che said.\n\n\"That day's you only had to be the you of that moment. That's enough,\" B Lin Che said.\n\nLittle Lin Che slowly, slowly lifted his head.\n\nFor the first time, his eyes looked directly at the two Lin Ches.\n\n\"Then... can I hug you?\"\n\nThe two Lin Ches froze.\n\nThen they crouched down at the same time and opened their arms.\n\nLittle Lin Che threw himself forward.\n\nThree Lin Ches, holding one another.\n\nIn that instant—\n\nSilvery-white light bloomed from among the three of them.\n\nThe light spread like ripples, sweeping across the entire playground.\n\nThe world of the memory began to brighten. So bright it hurt.\n\nThe children couldn't help but close their eyes.\n\nWhen they opened their eyes again—\n\nThey were back in the old auditorium.\n\nThe mirror was still there. But the cracks on its surface had shrunk.\n\nOnly a little. But they had truly shrunk.\n\n\"Look!\" A-Da rushed to the mirror.\n\nThe cracks were slowly, slowly closing toward the center.\n\nLike a wound healing.\n\n\"We did it!\" Xiao-Yang jumped up.\n\n\"Not yet,\" Hsiao-Yun said.\n\nShe pointed at the mirror. The cracks had closed halfway — and stopped.\n\nInside the mirror, the frozen playground was still there. Little Lin Che's hand was still raised halfway.\n\n\"There's one last step,\" Hsiao-Yun said. \"And that step isn't inside the mirror.\"\n\n\"Where is it?\" Ching-Ching asked.\n\nHsiao-Yun turned and looked at the two Lin Ches.\n\n\"It's inside yourselves.\"\n\nThe auditorium fell silent.\n\nChing-Ching looked down at her watch.\n\n\"11:20.\"\n\nThe two Lin Ches looked at each other from one step apart.\n\nThey both knew Hsiao-Yun was right.\n\nThe words not yet spoken, the thing not yet let go—\n\nIt was in both of their hearts.\n\n\"Next,\" B Lin Che said, his voice soft, \"it's our turn.\"\n\nLin Che nodded.\n\nThe two identical boys placed their hands over their hearts at the same time.\n\n\"There's still a mirror between us,\" B Lin Che said.\n\n\"Tonight, we shatter it,\" Lin Che said.\n\nThe sea breeze slipped through the gap under the auditorium door, making the mirror's surface gleam faintly.\n\n11:20.\n\nThe real battle was only now beginning.\n"},{"id":2,"rawContent":"# 第 18 章　兩種選擇\n\n十一點二十分。舊禮堂裡，安靜得只剩下呼吸聲。\n\n五十二個孩子退到牆邊，圍成一個大圈。\n\n圓圈中央，站著兩個林澈。\n\n「開始吧。」B 林澈說。\n\n林澈點頭。\n\n他們同時伸出手，握在一起。\n\n銀白色的光，從指縫間漫出來。\n\n可是這一次，他們沒有放開。\n\n記憶，像兩條河流，在兩隻手之間匯合。\n\n林澈看見了 B 林澈的全部。\n\n他看見一個男孩站在操場中央，笑得像太陽。所有人，繞著他轉。\n\n他看見那個男孩，半夜一個人躲在被子裡，練習明天要用的演講稿。\n\n他看見那個男孩摔倒了，全班都沒看見。他自己爬起來，拍拍褲子，繼續笑。\n\n他看見那個男孩，在鏡子裡看到自己的倒影時，說的第一句話不是「你好」，而是——\n\n「你累不累？」\n\n林澈的心，揪了一下。\n\nB 林澈，也看見了林澈的全部。\n\n他看見一個男孩坐在窗邊，看榕樹上的白頭翁，看了整整一個下課。\n\n他看見那個男孩，把每個同學的小習慣記在心裡：阿達喜歡轉筆，晴晴寫字時會皺左邊眉毛，小筠吃完飯會把便當盒擦得發亮。\n\n他看見那個男孩，站在舊禮堂的鏡子前面，被嚇得臉色發白，卻還是走了進去。\n\n他看見那個男孩，在夜裡寫下「想不起來也沒關係」，然後，又把那行字擦掉。\n\nB 林澈的鼻子，酸了。\n\n握在一起的手，開始發抖。\n\n「我……」A 林澈先開口。他的聲音，啞啞的。\n\n「我一直在羨慕你。」他說。\n\n禮堂裡，安靜得能聽見眼淚掉在地板上的聲音。\n\n「我每天都在想，」林澈的聲音在抖，「如果那天跑的人是我，如果全班叫的是我的名字，我會不會……過得比現在更好。」\n\n「我會不會，比較值得被喜歡。」\n\n孩子們的眼睛，紅了。\n\nB 林澈沒有馬上說話。他只是更用力地，握住林澈的手。\n\n「我也是。」B 林澈終於開口，「我也在羨慕你。」\n\n所有人都愣住了。\n\n「大家都看著我，」B 林澈說，「所以我不能停。跑步不能停，笑不能停，連難過，都要躲起來。」\n\n「我很累。可是我從來不敢說。因為全班，都靠我。」\n\n「每次看到你，」B 林澈看著他，「我都想——如果是我坐在窗邊看鳥，該有多好。」\n\n林澈的眼淚，掉了下來。\n\n「我們……」他哽咽著說，「我們一直在羨慕彼此。」\n\n「因為我們都只看見，自己沒有的那一半。」B 林澈說。\n\n兩個林澈，同時抬起頭。\n\n「你的世界，需要你的光。」A 林澈說。\n\n「你的世界，需要你的安靜。」B 林澈說。\n\n「你跑，我幫你看路。」A 林澈說。\n\n「你看，我幫你跑。」B 林澈說。\n\n然後，他們同時笑了。\n\n笑著笑著，又同時哭了。\n\n眼淚掉在握在一起的手上，溫溫的。\n\n「原來，」林澈說，「不是哪一種比較好。是我一直忘了——」\n\n「忘了什麼？」B 林澈問。\n\n「忘了，我已經是我了。」林澈說，「安靜的我，也是完整的我。」\n\nB 林澈用力點頭：「我也忘了。發光的我，也有權利喊累。」\n\n就在這一瞬間——\n\n銀白色的光，從他們握著的手裡，爆發出來。\n\n光沖上禮堂的屋頂，照亮了每一張臉。\n\n鏡面上的裂紋，像被光縫起來一樣，一道一道地消失。\n\n「裂紋在癒合！」阿達大喊。\n\n光持續了好幾秒。然後，慢慢地暗了下來。\n\n鏡面上，只剩下一道細細的線。像髮絲一樣細。\n\n「只剩最後一點點了！」B 晴晴說。\n\n小筠盯著鏡子。鏡子裡，那個靜止的操場還在。\n\n小小的林澈，還舉著半隻手。\n\n可是，這次不一樣了。\n\n他的眼睛，不再看著地面。\n\n他正看著他們。而且，他在笑。\n\n「最後一步，」小筠的聲音很輕，「是讓『那天』，自己完成。」\n\n「什麼意思？」阿達問。\n\n「我們一直想替他做決定。」小筠說，「舉手，還是不舉手。跑，還是不跑。」\n\n「可是現在，我們都懂了。」晴晴接著說，「不管他選哪一個，都很好。」\n\n「所以，」小筠看著大家，「我們要做的，是放手。讓那句話，自己說出口。」\n\n孩子們面面相覷。\n\n「讓那天，自己選。」林澈說。他的聲音，從來沒有這麼平靜過。\n\n「不管是哪一句話，」B 林澈說，「我們都已經準備好了。」\n\n兩個林澈，走到鏡子前。\n\n鏡子裡的小林澈，慢慢地、慢慢地，放下了舉到一半的手。\n\n不。不是放下。\n\n他把手，舉到了最高。\n\n然後——\n\n畫面，開始動了。\n\n劉老師走了過來。一步，兩步，三步。\n\n他張開嘴。\n\n聲音，從鏡子裡傳出來。\n\n不是一句。是兩句。\n\n兩句話，重疊在一起，同時響起：\n\n「你比較文靜，最後一棒，讓給跑得快的同學吧。」\n\n「你想試試看嗎？我看你可以。」\n\n兩句話，在禮堂裡迴盪。\n\n然後，鏡子裡的畫面，分成了兩個。\n\n左邊，小小的林澈退了回去。安安靜靜地，成了窗邊的影子。\n\n右邊，小小的林澈衝了出去。成了全班吶喊的英雄。\n\n兩個畫面，並排著，穩穩地，同時進行。\n\n沒有閃爍。沒有爭搶。沒有覆蓋。\n\n「兩個世界，都在了。」晴晴的聲音發抖。\n\n「誰都不用消失。」小筠說。眼鏡後面的眼睛，亮得嚇人。\n\n鏡面上的最後一道細線，慢慢地，消失了。\n\n鏡子，完好如初。\n\n可是鏡子裡，不再是一面普通的鏡子——\n\n裡面同時映著兩個世界，像一扇永遠開著的窗。\n\n孩子們看著鏡子，誰都沒有說話。\n\n然後，不知道是誰，先開始鼓掌的。\n\n掌聲，在舊禮堂裡迴盪。\n\n五十二個孩子，一邊鼓掌，一邊哭，一邊笑。\n\n林澈轉過身，看著大家。\n\n他忽然想起，那面鏡子第一次發光的那個黃昏。\n\n那個黃昏，他以為自己看到了一個「比自己更好的人」。\n\n現在他知道了。\n\n那個人，就是他自己。\n\n十一點四十分。\n\n而鏡子裡，兩個世界，都在發光。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 18 — Two Choices\n\n11:20 p.m. In the old auditorium, it was so quiet that only breathing could be heard.\n\nThe fifty-two children retreated to the walls, forming one great circle.\n\nIn the center of the circle stood the two Lin Ches.\n\n\"Let's begin,\" B Lin Che said.\n\nLin Che nodded.\n\nThey held out their hands at the same time and clasped them together.\n\nSilvery-white light seeped from between their fingers.\n\nBut this time, they did not let go.\n\nMemories, like two rivers, converged between their two hands.\n\nLin Che saw all of B Lin Che.\n\nHe saw a boy standing in the middle of the playground, smiling like the sun. Everyone circled around him.\n\nHe saw that boy, alone in the middle of the night, hiding under his blanket, practicing a speech for the next day.\n\nHe saw that boy fall, and no one in the class saw it. He picked himself up, dusted off his pants, and kept smiling.\n\nHe saw that boy, looking at his own reflection in the mirror, and the first thing he said wasn't \"hello,\" but—\n\n\"Aren't you tired?\"\n\nLin Che's heart clenched.\n\nB Lin Che saw all of Lin Che too.\n\nHe saw a boy sitting by the window, watching the white-eyes bird in the banyan tree for an entire recess.\n\nHe saw that boy quietly remembering every classmate's small habits: A-Da loves spinning his pen, Ching-Ching wrinkles her left eyebrow when writing, Hsiao-Yun polishes her lunch box until it gleams after every meal.\n\nHe saw that boy standing before the old auditorium's mirror, face white with fear — and still walking in.\n\nHe saw that boy writing \"it's okay if I never remember\" late at night, and then erasing the words.\n\nB Lin Che's nose stung.\n\nThe clasped hands began to tremble.\n\n\"I...\" A Lin Che spoke first. His voice was hoarse.\n\n\"I've always been envious of you,\" he said.\n\nThe auditorium was so quiet you could hear tears hitting the floor.\n\n\"I think about it every day,\" Lin Che's voice shook. \"If I'd been the one who ran that day, if the whole class had shouted MY name — would I... be living a better life than now?\"\n\n\"Would I be... more worth liking?\"\n\nThe children's eyes reddened.\n\nB Lin Che didn't speak right away. He just gripped Lin Che's hand harder.\n\n\"Me too,\" B Lin Che finally said. \"I envy you too.\"\n\nEveryone froze.\n\n\"Everyone looks at me,\" B Lin Che said. \"So I can't stop. I can't stop running, can't stop smiling. Even my sadness has to hide.\"\n\n\"I'm so tired. But I never dared say it, because the whole class depends on me.\"\n\n\"Every time I see you,\" B Lin Che looked at him, \"I think — what if it were me sitting by the window, watching the birds? How nice that would be.\"\n\nLin Che's tears fell.\n\n\"We...\" he choked out. \"We've been envying each other all along.\"\n\n\"Because we both only saw the half we didn't have,\" B Lin Che said.\n\nThe two Lin Ches lifted their heads at the same time.\n\n\"Your world needs your light,\" A Lin Che said.\n\n\"Your world needs your quiet,\" B Lin Che said.\n\n\"You run, and I'll watch the road for you,\" A Lin Che said.\n\n\"You watch, and I'll run for you,\" B Lin Che said.\n\nThen, they smiled at the same time.\n\nAnd as they smiled, they cried at the same time.\n\nThe tears fell onto their clasped hands, warm.\n\n\"So,\" Lin Che said, \"it's not that one way is better. It's that I kept forgetting—\"\n\n\"Forgetting what?\" B Lin Che asked.\n\n\"Forgetting that I'm already me.\" Lin Che said. \"The quiet me is a complete me too.\"\n\nB Lin Che nodded hard: \"I forgot too. The shining me also has the right to say I'm tired.\"\n\nAt that very instant—\n\nSilvery-white light erupted from their clasped hands.\n\nThe light shot up to the auditorium roof, illuminating every face.\n\nThe cracks on the mirror's surface vanished one by one, as if stitched shut by the light.\n\n\"The cracks are healing!\" A-Da shouted.\n\nThe light lasted for several seconds. Then, it slowly dimmed.\n\nOn the mirror's surface, only one thin line remained. Fine as a strand of hair.\n\n\"Only a tiny bit left!\" B Ching-Ching said.\n\nHsiao-Yun stared at the mirror. Inside it, the frozen playground was still there.\n\nLittle Lin Che still held his hand halfway up.\n\nBut this time, it was different.\n\nHis eyes no longer looked at the ground.\n\nHe was looking at them. And he was smiling.\n\n\"The last step,\" Hsiao-Yun's voice was soft, \"is to let 'that day' complete itself.\"\n\n\"What do you mean?\" A-Da asked.\n\n\"We've been trying to make the decision for him,\" Hsiao-Yun said. \"To raise the hand or not. To run or not.\"\n\n\"But now, we all understand,\" Ching-Ching picked up. \"Whichever one he chooses, it's fine.\"\n\n\"So,\" Hsiao-Yun looked at everyone, \"what we have to do is let go. Let that sentence speak itself.\"\n\nThe children looked at one another.\n\n\"Let that day choose for itself,\" Lin Che said. His voice had never been so calm.\n\n\"Whichever sentence it is,\" B Lin Che said, \"we're ready now.\"\n\nThe two Lin Ches walked up to the mirror.\n\nIn the mirror, little Lin Che slowly, slowly lowered his half-raised hand.\n\nNo. He didn't lower it.\n\nHe raised it to its very highest.\n\nThen—\n\nThe scene began to move.\n\nCoach Liu walked over. One step, two steps, three steps.\n\nHe opened his mouth.\n\nA voice came from the mirror.\n\nNot one sentence. Two.\n\nTwo sentences, overlapping, sounding at the same time:\n\n\"You're more on the quiet side. For the anchor leg, leave it to the kids who run fast.\"\n\n\"Don't you want to give it a try? I think you can do it.\"\n\nThe two sentences echoed through the auditorium.\n\nThen, the image in the mirror split into two.\n\nOn the left, little Lin Che stepped back. Quietly, he became the shadow by the window.\n\nOn the right, little Lin Che sprinted out. He became the hero the whole class cheered for.\n\nTwo images, side by side, steady, playing at the same time.\n\nNo flickering. No fighting. No overwriting.\n\n\"Both worlds are here now,\" Ching-Ching's voice trembled.\n\n\"No one has to disappear,\" Hsiao-Yun said, her eyes gleaming fiercely behind her glasses.\n\nThe last thin line on the mirror's surface slowly vanished.\n\nThe mirror was whole again.\n\nBut it was no longer an ordinary mirror—\n\nIt reflected both worlds at once, like a window that would never close.\n\nThe children looked at the mirror, no one speaking.\n\nThen, no one knew who started clapping first.\n\nThe applause echoed through the old auditorium.\n\nThe fifty-two children clapped, and cried, and laughed, all at once.\n\nLin Che turned and looked at everyone.\n\nHe suddenly remembered the dusk when the mirror first glowed.\n\nThat dusk, he thought he'd seen \"someone better than him.\"\n\nNow he knew.\n\nThat person was himself.\n\n11:40 p.m.\n\nAnd inside the mirror, both worlds were glowing.\n"},{"id":3,"rawContent":"# 第 19 章　最後的同學會\n\n十一點四十分。掌聲停下來之後，舊禮堂裡一片安靜。\n\n「成功了……嗎？」阿達小聲問。\n\n「成功了。」晴晴說。她的聲音有點抖，「兩個世界，都還在。」\n\n忽然，阿寶指著 B 阿寶：「那現在，我可以碰到你嗎？」\n\n所有人愣住。\n\nB 阿寶走過來，伸出一根手指。\n\n兩根手指，輕輕碰在一起。\n\n什麼都沒有發生。\n\n沒有記憶交換。沒有同步。沒有變淡。\n\n「耶——！」阿寶跳起來，「我們可以碰對方了！」\n\n孩子們歡呼起來。兩個世界的人，開始互相擁抱、擊掌、搥肩膀。\n\n五十二個人，笑成一團。\n\n林澈和 B 林澈，握著手，也笑了。\n\n只有小筠沒有笑。\n\n她站在鏡子前，盯著它看。\n\n「你們有沒有發現，」她忽然說，「鏡子的光，在變。」\n\n孩子們安靜下來。\n\n鏡面的銀白色光芒，還是很亮。可是，好像比剛才……淡了一點點。\n\n「它在變暗。」晴晴走過來。\n\n「為什麼？我們不是成功了嗎？」阿達急了。\n\n「七天。」小筠說，聲音很輕，「鏡子，只開七天。」\n\n「三十年前，也是這樣。七天一到，就停了。」\n\n孩子們你看看我，我看看你。\n\n「所以……」小陽的聲音有點乾，「午夜一到，鏡子就會關上？」\n\n「嗯。」小筠點頭，「而且，這次關上之後——」\n\n她沒有說下去。\n\n可是大家都懂。三十年前，禮堂封了三十年。\n\n今晚，是最後一次。\n\n快樂的氣氛，像退潮一樣，慢慢地退了。\n\n「別那麼喪氣啦！」達哥忽然大喊。他跳到椅子上，「我們不是早就知道今天是最後一天嗎？」\n\n「就是啊！」小陽也喊，「我們本來，就是要道別的！」\n\n「對！」孩子們附和。\n\n「所以，」達哥舉起手裡的紙——那張畫滿流程圖的紙，「我們不是還有『兩個世界的同學會』嗎？」\n\n「最後的二十分鐘，要笑著過完！」小陽喊。\n\n孩子們的眼睛，重新亮了起來。\n\n「同學會！同學會！」五十二個聲音一起喊。\n\n「可是，鏡子前不能亂跑。」晴晴立刻進入班長模式，「第一組負責佈置，第二組負責零食，第三組——」\n\n「交換卡片！」阿達大喊，「不要忘了我的點子！」\n\n「對！交換卡片！」達哥拍手，「大家把想對另一個世界的人說的話，寫在卡片上！」\n\n孩子們立刻忙起來。\n\n安安和 B 安安負責畫卡片。兩個女生頭碰頭，一眨眼就畫出滿地的小卡片。\n\n小筠和 B 小筠負責寫。一個寫字，一個畫插圖，配合得天衣無縫。\n\n阿達和達哥負責發卡片。兩個人在人群裡鑽來鑽去，像兩條魚。\n\n晴晴和 B 晴晴負責排桌椅。兩個班長不用說話，默契好得嚇人。\n\n小陽負責氣氛。他站在桌子上，指揮大家唱歌。\n\n林澈和 B 林澈，站在鏡子前，看著這一切。\n\n「很美吧？」B 林澈說。\n\n「嗯。」林澈點頭。\n\n他忽然從口袋裡，拿出那支藍色鉛筆。\n\n「這支筆，」他說，「是在海聲書店買的。」\n\n「我們那邊的海聲書店。」他頓了一下，「它消失過。現在，又回來了。」\n\nB 林澈看著那支筆，笑了。\n\n「你們的世界，會越來越好的。」他說。\n\n「你們也是。」林澈說。\n\n兩個少年，並肩站著，看著兩班的孩子們忙進忙出。\n\n阿達一個人躲到角落，從口袋裡拿出那顆草莓。\n\n草莓還是很紅。在昏暗的禮堂裡，像一顆小小的燈。\n\n「喂。」達哥忽然出現，蹲在他旁邊。\n\n「你捨不得吃喔？」達哥笑。\n\n「嗯。」阿達點頭。\n\n「傻瓜。」達哥說，「草莓不吃會壞掉的。我們那邊的草莓，明天就要結果了。」\n\n他停了停：「而且，我明天會去摘新的。」\n\n阿達張了張嘴。\n\n「達哥，」他小聲說，「鏡子關了以後，我們……是不是就再也見不到了？」\n\n達哥沒有回答。\n\n過了一會，達哥拍拍他的背，站起來。\n\n「誰知道呢。」他笑，「也許三十年前那批小孩，也說過同樣的話。」\n\n「可是你看，」達哥指著鏡子，「三十年後，它又開了。」\n\n阿達順著他的手，看向鏡子。\n\n銀白色的光，溫柔地流動著。裡面有兩個世界。\n\n「所以，」達哥的聲音很輕，「也許哪一天，我們自己也說不定，會再見到面。」\n\n阿達把草莓放回口袋，放得很小心。\n\n「那我把它留著。」他說，「留到下一次。」\n\n「好。」達哥伸出手。\n\n兩隻手，用力地握了一下。\n\n沒有光。沒有記憶交換。\n\n只有掌心的溫度。\n\n十一點五十分。\n\n同學會，開始了。\n\n禮堂裡，燈光昏暗。五十二個孩子圍成一圈。\n\n小陽站在中間，舉起一瓶果汁。\n\n「敬兩個世界！」他喊。\n\n「敬兩個世界！」五十二個聲音。\n\n「敬今天！」\n\n「敬今天！」\n\n「敬我們！」\n\n「敬我們——！」\n\n孩子們碰杯。果汁灑得到處都是，也沒有人在意。\n\n交換卡片，開始了。\n\n阿寶把卡片塞給 B 阿寶，上面寫著：「對不起，還有，謝謝。」\n\nB 阿寶把卡片塞回給他：「下次，來我們的世界吃養樂多。」\n\n安安收到 B 安安的卡片，上面畫著兩個女生牽著手。\n\n小筠收到 B 小筠的卡片，上面寫著：「你永遠是我最好的搭檔。」\n\n晴晴收到 B 晴晴的卡片：「嚴肅的班長，也要記得笑。」\n\n小陽收到晴晴的卡片：「你的笑聲，很大聲。很好聽。」\n\n每個人都在笑。每個人，都在哭。\n\n阿達把卡片塞給達哥。卡片上，密密麻麻寫滿了字。最後一行是：\n\n「謝謝你，讓我被看見。」\n\n達哥看著卡片，笑了。他張開嘴，想說什麼——\n\n就在這時，鏡子的光，突然一閃。\n\n孩子們全都停下動作。\n\n銀白色的光，慢慢地、慢慢地，暗了下去。\n\n像一盞燈，被輕輕地吹熄。\n\n「鏡子……」晴晴的聲音發抖，「要關了。」\n\n十一點五十五分。\n\n剩下的時間，不多了。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 19 — The Final Class Reunion\n\n11:40 p.m. After the applause died down, the old auditorium fell silent.\n\n\"Did we... do it?\" A-Da asked quietly.\n\n\"We did it,\" Ching-Ching said. Her voice trembled a little. \"Both worlds are still here.\"\n\nSuddenly, A-Bao pointed at B A-Bao: \"So now... can I touch you?\"\n\nEveryone froze.\n\nB A-Bao walked over and held out one finger.\n\nThe two fingertips touched, ever so lightly.\n\nNothing happened.\n\nNo memory exchange. No syncing. No fading.\n\n\"Yay—!\" A-Bao jumped up. \"We can touch each other now!\"\n\nThe children cheered. People from the two worlds began hugging, high-fiving, and thumping shoulders.\n\nThe fifty-two of them dissolved into laughter.\n\nLin Che and B Lin Che, still holding hands, laughed too.\n\nOnly Hsiao-Yun didn't laugh.\n\nShe stood in front of the mirror, staring at it.\n\n\"Have you noticed,\" she suddenly said, \"the mirror's light is changing?\"\n\nThe children fell quiet.\n\nThe silvery-white glow on the mirror was still bright. But it seemed... a little fainter than before.\n\n\"It's dimming,\" Ching-Ching walked over.\n\n\"Why? Didn't we succeed?\" A-Da grew anxious.\n\n\"Seven days,\" Hsiao-Yun said, her voice soft. \"The mirror only opens for seven days.\"\n\n\"It was the same thirty years ago. Once seven days passed, it stopped.\"\n\nThe children looked at one another.\n\n\"So...\" Xiao-Yang's voice was a little dry. \"The moment midnight comes, the mirror will close?\"\n\n\"Mm.\" Hsiao-Yun nodded. \"And after it closes this time—\"\n\nShe didn't finish the sentence.\n\nBut everyone understood. Thirty years ago, the auditorium had been sealed for thirty years.\n\nTonight was the last time.\n\nThe joyful mood ebbed away, like a tide going out.\n\n\"Don't be so gloomy!\" Da-ge suddenly shouted, jumping onto a chair. \"Didn't we know from the start that today was the last day?\"\n\n\"That's right!\" Xiao-Yang shouted too. \"We were always going to say goodbye!\"\n\n\"Yeah!\" the children chimed in.\n\n\"So,\" Da-ge raised the paper in his hand — the one covered in flowcharts, \"don't we still have the 'Two-Worlds Class Reunion'?\"\n\n\"The last twenty minutes, we're spending them laughing!\" Xiao-Yang shouted.\n\nThe children's eyes lit up again.\n\n\"Reunion! Reunion!\" Fifty-two voices shouted together.\n\n\"But no running wild in front of the mirror.\" Ching-Ching instantly went into class-monitor mode. \"Group One handles decorations, Group Two handles snacks, Group Three—\"\n\n\"Card exchange!\" A-Da shouted. \"Don't forget my idea!\"\n\n\"Right! Card exchange!\" Da-ge clapped. \"Everyone write down what you want to say to the people in the other world!\"\n\nThe children immediately got busy.\n\nAn-An and B An-An were in charge of making the cards. The two girls put their heads together and produced little cards all over the floor in the blink of an eye.\n\nHsiao-Yun and B Hsiao-Yun were in charge of writing. One wrote the words, the other drew illustrations — they worked together flawlessly.\n\nA-Da and Da-ge were in charge of handing out the cards. The two of them weaved through the crowd like a pair of fish.\n\nChing-Ching and B Ching-Ching were in charge of arranging the tables and chairs. The two monitors didn't need to speak — their coordination was frighteningly smooth.\n\nXiao-Yang was in charge of the mood. He stood on a table, directing everyone in song.\n\nLin Che and B Lin Che stood before the mirror, watching it all.\n\n\"Beautiful, isn't it?\" B Lin Che said.\n\n\"Mm.\" Lin Che nodded.\n\nHe suddenly pulled the blue pencil out of his pocket.\n\n\"This pencil,\" he said, \"I bought it at Haisheng Bookstore.\"\n\n\"OUR Haisheng Bookstore.\" He paused. \"It disappeared once. And now, it's come back.\"\n\nB Lin Che looked at the pencil and smiled.\n\n\"Your world will get better and better,\" he said.\n\n\"Yours too,\" Lin Che said.\n\nThe two boys stood side by side, watching the children of both classes bustle about.\n\nA-Da slipped off to a corner by himself and took the strawberry out of his pocket.\n\nThe strawberry was still very red. In the dim auditorium, it glowed like a tiny lamp.\n\n\"Hey.\" Da-ge suddenly appeared and crouched down beside him.\n\n\"You can't bear to eat it?\" Da-ge grinned.\n\n\"Mm.\" A-Da nodded.\n\n\"Silly.\" Da-ge said. \"Strawberries go bad if you don't eat them. Our strawberries are going to bear fruit again tomorrow.\"\n\nHe paused: \"And I'll go pick new ones tomorrow.\"\n\nA-Da opened his mouth.\n\n\"Da-ge,\" he said quietly, \"after the mirror closes... will we never see each other again?\"\n\nDa-ge didn't answer.\n\nAfter a while, Da-ge patted his back and stood up.\n\n\"Who knows.\" He smiled. \"Maybe the kids from thirty years ago said the same thing.\"\n\n\"But look,\" Da-ge pointed at the mirror, \"thirty years later, it opened again.\"\n\nA-Da followed his hand and looked at the mirror.\n\nThe silvery-white light flowed gently. Inside it were two worlds.\n\n\"So,\" Da-ge's voice was soft, \"maybe one day, we ourselves — who knows — might meet again.\"\n\nA-Da put the strawberry back in his pocket, very carefully.\n\n\"Then I'll save it,\" he said. \"For next time.\"\n\n\"Okay.\" Da-ge held out his hand.\n\nThe two hands shook firmly.\n\nNo light. No memory exchange.\n\nOnly the warmth of the palm.\n\n11:50 p.m.\n\nThe reunion began.\n\nIn the auditorium, the light was dim. The fifty-two children formed a circle.\n\nXiao-Yang stood in the middle and raised a bottle of juice.\n\n\"To the two worlds!\" he shouted.\n\n\"To the two worlds!\" fifty-two voices answered.\n\n\"To today!\"\n\n\"To today!\"\n\n\"To us!\"\n\n\"To us—!\"\n\nThe children clinked their bottles. Juice spilled everywhere, and no one cared.\n\nThe card exchange began.\n\nA-Bao pressed his card into B A-Bao's hands. It read: \"Sorry. And, thank you.\"\n\nB A-Bao pressed his card back: \"Next time, come eat Yakult in our world.\"\n\nAn-An received B An-An's card, on which two girls were drawn holding hands.\n\nHsiao-Yun received B Hsiao-Yun's card. It read: \"You'll always be my best partner.\"\n\nChing-Ching received B Ching-Ching's card: \"Even a serious monitor should remember to smile.\"\n\nXiao-Yang received Ching-Ching's card: \"Your laugh is very loud. It sounds very nice.\"\n\nEveryone was smiling. Everyone was crying.\n\nA-Da pressed his card into Da-ge's hands. The card was packed with writing. The last line was:\n\n\"Thank you for letting me be seen.\"\n\nDa-ge looked at the card and smiled. He opened his mouth, about to say something—\n\nJust then, the mirror's light suddenly flickered.\n\nAll the children stopped what they were doing.\n\nThe silvery-white light slowly, slowly dimmed.\n\nLike a lamp being gently blown out.\n\n\"The mirror...\" Ching-Ching's voice trembled. \"It's closing.\"\n\n11:55 p.m.\n\nThere wasn't much time left.\n"},{"id":4,"rawContent":"# 第 20 章　道別開始\n\n十一點五十五分。鏡子的光，已經暗得像黃昏的霧。\n\n「B 世界的人，快！」晴晴站在鏡子旁，大聲喊，「一個一個過，不要擠！」\n\n孩子們立刻排成一列。\n\n每一個人經過鏡子的時候，都會停一下，回頭看一眼。\n\nB 晴晴走到晴晴面前。兩個班長，面對面。\n\n「嚴肅的班長，」B 晴晴笑，「記得笑。」\n\n「隨便的班長，」晴晴也笑了，眼睛卻紅紅的，「記得嚴肅。」\n\n兩個人，用力地抱了一下。\n\n然後，B 晴晴走進鏡子裡。\n\nB 小筠走到小筠面前，把一張紙條塞進她手裡。\n\n小筠低頭一看——是新的紙條。上面畫著兩個小人。這次，它們在揮手。\n\n「再見，我的搭檔。」B 小筠說。\n\n「再見。」小筠說。她沒有哭。可是她的眼鏡，霧了。\n\nB 安安和安安抱在一起，抱了很久。\n\n「繼續畫。」B 安安說。\n\n「嗯。」安安點頭，「畫給全世界看。」\n\nB 阿寶衝過來，把一罐養樂多塞給阿寶。\n\n「最後一罐！我們世界的！」他喊。\n\n阿寶接住，愣了一秒，然後大喊：「我、我會喝完它的！然後把空罐子留著！」\n\n大家都笑了。笑著笑著，眼淚掉得更兇。\n\n一個一個，B 世界的孩子走進鏡子裡。\n\n小陽是最後幾個。他走到晴晴面前。\n\n「喂，」小陽說，「你的卡片，我會貼在我的床頭。」\n\n「你的笑聲，」晴晴說，「我會記得很久。」\n\n小陽笑了。那個大大的、會傳遍整個走廊的笑聲，又響了一次。\n\n然後，他也走進了鏡子裡。\n\n現在，只剩下 B 林澈和達哥了。\n\n達哥走到阿達面前。\n\n「卡片，我收到了。」達哥說，眼睛亮亮的，「我把它，放在我們教室的佈告欄上了。」\n\n阿達張了張嘴。\n\n「達哥，我……」他的聲音卡住了。\n\n他想說的話，在喉嚨裡轉了一百圈，就是出不來。\n\n達哥看著他，忽然張開雙臂。\n\n「抱一下吧。」他說，「當作……下一次見面的預約。」\n\n阿達撲上去，用力抱住他。\n\n沒有光。沒有記憶交換。只有兩個人的心跳。\n\n然後，達哥鬆開手，退後一步，走進了鏡子裡。\n\n阿達站在原地，一動也不動。\n\nB 林澈，最後一個。\n\n他走到林澈面前。\n\n兩個一模一樣的少年，面對面。\n\n「謝謝你。」B 林澈說，「謝謝你，讓我看到安靜的力量。」\n\n「謝謝你。」林澈說，「謝謝你，讓我看到發光的勇氣。」\n\n「我們，誰都不是誰的『比較好』。」B 林澈說。\n\n「我們，是彼此的另外一半。」林澈說。\n\n兩個林澈，伸出拳頭，輕輕碰了一下。\n\n「再見。」B 林澈說。\n\n「不。」林澈說，「是『下次見』。」\n\nB 林澈笑了。他轉過身，走進鏡子裡。\n\n銀光盪了一下。然後，恢復平靜。\n\n舊禮堂裡，只剩下二十六個 A 世界的孩子。\n\n還有，一面越來越暗的鏡子。\n\n安靜了很久。\n\n「結束了嗎……」小美小聲問。\n\n「還沒有。」晴晴說，「鏡子還沒完全關上。在它關上之前，我們都要待在這裡。」\n\n孩子們在禮堂裡坐下。沒有人想回家。\n\n林澈走到阿達身邊。阿達還站在鏡子前，動也不動。\n\n「阿達？」林澈輕輕叫他。\n\n阿達沒有回頭。他的眼睛，盯著鏡子裡那片模糊的銀光。\n\n「林澈。」阿達的聲音，啞啞的，「如果……如果我想過去呢？」\n\n林澈愣住。\n\n「過去哪裡？」\n\n「B 世界。」阿達說。\n\n禮堂裡，忽然安靜下來。\n\n所有人都聽到了。\n\n「你瘋了嗎？」阿寶跳起來，「鏡子就快關了！過去，就回不來了！」\n\n「我知道。」阿達說。\n\n他轉過身。他的眼睛，紅紅的，卻很亮。\n\n「我一直在想，」他說，「在我們這邊，我是那個講笑話被叫『安靜』的阿達。」\n\n「可是在那邊，我是達哥。是被大家聽、被大家信賴、被大家叫『達哥』的達哥。」\n\n「我寫過一張紙條，」他的聲音在抖，「上面寫著『想留下』。然後，我把那張紙，丟進了垃圾桶。」\n\n「因為我覺得，這樣太自私了。」\n\n孩子們安靜地聽著。\n\n「可是剛才，達哥抱住我的時候，」阿達說，「我忽然想——」\n\n「也許，留下來不是自私。也許，是勇敢。」\n\n沒人說話。\n\n晴晴站起來，走到他面前。\n\n「阿達。」她說，「你想清楚了嗎？」\n\n阿達看著她，用力點頭。\n\n「我想清楚了。」他說，「我想過去。」\n\n「不是因為我們的世界不好。」他的聲音穩了下來，「是因為，那邊有一個位置，是空的。」\n\n「一個叫『吳達』的位置。而那個位置，是我。」\n\n禮堂裡，響起一陣抽氣聲。\n\n林澈看著阿達。他想起操場上，那個追著自己跑的、大喊「林澈！林澈！」的阿達。\n\n他想起阿達說：「你只是還沒被看見。」\n\n他明白了。阿達說這句話的時候，說的，也許不只是林澈。\n\n晴晴低頭看手錶。\n\n「十一點五十七分。」\n\n阿達走到鏡子前。銀白色的光，已經暗得像一層薄霧。\n\n他慢慢地，抬起手。\n\n就在他的指尖，碰到鏡面的那一瞬間——\n\n鏡子裡，忽然亮起了一點光。\n\n像一顆星星，在霧裡，閃了一下。\n\n「達哥？」阿達瞪大眼睛。\n\n鏡子的另一邊，達哥的臉，出現在霧裡。\n\n他在笑。\n\n他的手，也按在鏡面上。隔著一層薄薄的銀光，跟阿達的手，貼在一起。\n\n「我聽到了。」達哥說，「你們講的話，鏡子都傳過來了。」\n\n「所以，」他笑了，眼睛裡有淚光，「我有一個提議。」\n\n禮堂裡，所有人都屏住了呼吸。\n\n達哥的聲音，穿過銀霧，清清楚楚地傳了過來：\n\n「我們，交換吧。」\n\n「你來我的世界，被看見。」\n\n「我去你的世界，讓別人被看見。」\n\n十一點五十八分。\n\n而鏡子的光，還在慢慢、慢慢地，暗下去。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 20 — The Farewell Begins\n\n11:55 p.m. The mirror's light had dimmed to the haze of dusk.\n\n\"World B, hurry!\" Ching-Ching stood by the mirror, shouting. \"One at a time, no pushing!\"\n\nThe children immediately lined up.\n\nEach one, as they passed the mirror, paused and glanced back.\n\nB Ching-Ching walked up to Ching-Ching. The two monitors stood face to face.\n\n\"Serious monitor,\" B Ching-Ching smiled, \"remember to smile.\"\n\n\"Carefree monitor,\" Ching-Ching smiled too, though her eyes were red, \"remember to be serious.\"\n\nThe two of them hugged tightly.\n\nThen B Ching-Ching walked into the mirror.\n\nB Hsiao-Yun walked up to Hsiao-Yun and pressed a note into her hand.\n\nHsiao-Yun looked down — a new note. It had two little stick figures. This time, they were waving.\n\n\"Goodbye, my partner,\" B Hsiao-Yun said.\n\n\"Goodbye,\" Hsiao-Yun said. She didn't cry. But her glasses fogged up.\n\nB An-An and An-An hugged, and held on for a long time.\n\n\"Keep drawing,\" B An-An said.\n\n\"Mm.\" An-An nodded. \"I'll draw for the whole world to see.\"\n\nB A-Bao rushed over and shoved a bottle of Yakult into A-Bao's hands.\n\n\"The last one! From our world!\" he shouted.\n\nA-Bao caught it, froze for a second, then yelled: \"I-I'll drink it all! And keep the empty bottle!\"\n\nEveryone laughed. And as they laughed, the tears fell harder.\n\nOne by one, the children of World B walked into the mirror.\n\nXiao-Yang was among the last few. He walked up to Ching-Ching.\n\n\"Hey,\" Xiao-Yang said, \"your card — I'm putting it on my headboard.\"\n\n\"Your laugh,\" Ching-Ching said, \"I'll remember it for a long time.\"\n\nXiao-Yang smiled. That huge laugh of his — the one that carried through the whole hallway — rang out once more.\n\nThen he, too, walked into the mirror.\n\nNow only B Lin Che and Da-ge remained.\n\nDa-ge walked up to A-Da.\n\n\"The card,\" Da-ge said, his eyes bright. \"I got it. I put it up on our class bulletin board.\"\n\nA-Da opened his mouth.\n\n\"Da-ge, I...\" His voice caught.\n\nThe words he wanted to say spun a hundred circles in his throat, but couldn't come out.\n\nDa-ge looked at him and suddenly opened his arms.\n\n\"Let's hug,\" he said. \"Think of it as... a reservation for our next meeting.\"\n\nA-Da threw himself forward and hugged him tight.\n\nNo light. No memory exchange. Only two heartbeats.\n\nThen Da-ge let go, stepped back, and walked into the mirror.\n\nA-Da stood where he was, not moving at all.\n\nB Lin Che was the last one.\n\nHe walked up to Lin Che.\n\nTwo identical boys, face to face.\n\n\"Thank you,\" B Lin Che said. \"Thank you for showing me the power of quiet.\"\n\n\"Thank you,\" Lin Che said. \"Thank you for showing me the courage to shine.\"\n\n\"Neither of us is the 'better one,'\" B Lin Che said.\n\n\"We are each other's other half,\" Lin Che said.\n\nThe two Lin Ches extended their fists and bumped them lightly.\n\n\"Goodbye,\" B Lin Che said.\n\n\"No,\" Lin Che said. \"It's 'see you next time.'\"\n\nB Lin Che smiled. He turned and walked into the mirror.\n\nThe silver light rippled once. Then it settled.\n\nIn the old auditorium, only the twenty-six children of World A remained.\n\nAnd a mirror growing dimmer and dimmer.\n\nThe silence lasted a long time.\n\n\"Is it over...\" Hsiao-Mei asked quietly.\n\n\"Not yet,\" Ching-Ching said. \"The mirror hasn't fully closed. Until it does, we all stay here.\"\n\nThe children sat down in the auditorium. No one wanted to go home.\n\nLin Che walked over to A-Da. A-Da still stood before the mirror, motionless.\n\n\"A-Da?\" Lin Che called softly.\n\nA-Da didn't turn around. His eyes were fixed on the blurry silver light in the mirror.\n\n\"Lin Che.\" A-Da's voice was hoarse. \"What if... what if I want to go over?\"\n\nLin Che froze.\n\n\"Go over where?\"\n\n\"World B,\" A-Da said.\n\nThe auditorium suddenly fell silent.\n\nEveryone had heard.\n\n\"Are you crazy?\" A-Bao jumped up. \"The mirror's about to close! Once you go over, you can't come back!\"\n\n\"I know,\" A-Da said.\n\nHe turned around. His eyes were red, but bright.\n\n\"I keep thinking,\" he said, \"on our side, I'm the A-Da whose jokes get him told to 'be quiet.'\"\n\n\"But over there, I'm Da-ge. The Da-ge everyone listens to, everyone trusts, everyone calls 'Da-ge.'\"\n\n\"I wrote a note once,\" his voice trembled, \"with the words 'I want to stay.' Then I threw it into the trash can.\"\n\n\"Because I thought that was too selfish.\"\n\nThe children listened quietly.\n\n\"But just now, when Da-ge hugged me,\" A-Da said, \"I suddenly thought—\"\n\n\"Maybe staying isn't selfish. Maybe it's brave.\"\n\nNo one spoke.\n\nChing-Ching stood up and walked over to him.\n\n\"A-Da,\" she said. \"Have you really thought this through?\"\n\nA-Da looked at her and nodded firmly.\n\n\"I've thought it through,\" he said. \"I want to go over.\"\n\n\"It's not because our world is bad.\" His voice steadied. \"It's because there's an empty spot over there.\"\n\n\"A spot named 'Wu Da.' And that spot is me.\"\n\nA collective gasp rose in the auditorium.\n\nLin Che looked at A-Da. He remembered the A-Da who'd chased him around the playground, shouting \"Lin Che! Lin Che!\"\n\nHe remembered A-Da saying: \"You're just someone who hasn't been seen yet.\"\n\nHe understood now. When A-Da said that, he hadn't only meant Lin Che.\n\nChing-Ching looked down at her watch.\n\n\"11:57.\"\n\nA-Da walked up to the mirror. The silvery-white light had dimmed to a thin mist.\n\nHe slowly raised his hand.\n\nThe instant his fingertip touched the mirror's surface—\n\nInside the mirror, a point of light suddenly lit up.\n\nLike a star flashing once in the fog.\n\n\"Da-ge?\" A-Da's eyes went wide.\n\nOn the other side of the mirror, Da-ge's face appeared in the mist.\n\nHe was smiling.\n\nHis hand pressed against the mirror too, separated from A-Da's by a thin layer of silver light.\n\n\"I heard you,\" Da-ge said. \"The mirror carried your words over.\"\n\n\"So,\" he smiled, tears glistening in his eyes, \"I have a proposal.\"\n\nEveryone in the auditorium held their breath.\n\nDa-ge's voice came through the silver mist, clear and distinct:\n\n\"Let's swap.\"\n\n\"You come to my world, and be seen.\"\n\n\"I go to your world, and help others be seen.\"\n\n11:58 p.m.\n\nAnd the mirror's light was still slowly, slowly dimming.\n"},{"id":5,"rawContent":"# 第 21 章　交換\n\n十一點五十八分。達哥的話，還在禮堂裡迴盪。\n\n「交換？」阿達瞪大眼睛，隔著銀霧，看著那張跟自己一模一樣的臉。\n\n「交換。」達哥笑，「你跟我，有同一顆腦袋。你在我的世界，會做得比我好。我去你的世界，也會被需要的。」\n\n「可是……」阿達的聲音在抖，「你的世界，大家都喜歡你。你為什麼……」\n\n「因為，」達哥說，「我也想知道，自己離開了掌聲，還能不能讓別人笑出來。」\n\n他停了停：「而且，我想去幫你的世界。讓那裡的人知道，吳達的點子，值得被聽。」\n\n阿達的眼淚，掉了下來。\n\n「你這個笨蛋……」他笑，眼淚一直掉，「你真的是……全世界最帥的我。」\n\n達哥大笑：「廢話！我們同一張臉！」\n\n孩子們都笑了。笑著笑著，眼睛都紅了。\n\n「好。」阿達擦掉眼淚，「我跟你換。」\n\n他轉過身，面對二十六個 A 世界的同學。\n\n「各位。」他說，「我要走了。」\n\n沒人說話。\n\n阿達一個一個看過去。小美、鐵牛、子涵、阿寶……\n\n「阿寶。」他忽然說，「以後我的座位，就交給你保管了。抽屜裡的彈珠，都是你的。」\n\n阿寶的眼眶，瞬間紅了。\n\n「誰、誰要你的彈珠！」他吼，聲音卻抖得不行。\n\n「還有你，小美。」阿達說，「你下次哭的時候，記得，笑話第一名阿達不在了，可是笑話，會留下來。」\n\n小美「哇」地一聲，哭了出來。\n\n「阿達……」子涵小聲說，「對不起。我上次說你的企劃很無聊……」\n\n「道什麼歉啊！」阿達笑，「你們這些傢伙，現在才知道要捨不得我！」\n\n孩子們圍了過來。\n\n晴晴走到他面前。\n\n兩個人，一個是全班最嚴肅的人，一個是全班最吵的人。\n\n「吳達。」晴晴說。\n\n「幹嘛？」阿達挺起胸膛，「要罵我嗎？最後一次了喔！」\n\n晴晴看著他。她的眼睛，紅紅的。\n\n「對不起。」她說，「我每次都叫你安靜。」\n\n阿達愣住了。\n\n「你的點子，其實都很好。」晴晴說，「是我太急著管秩序，忘了聽你說。」\n\n眼淚，從阿達臉上滑下來。\n\n「你這……」他的聲音哽住了，「你這句話，我等了六年。」\n\n晴晴的眼淚，也掉了下來。\n\n兩個人，在昏暗的禮堂裡，用力地抱了一下。\n\n最後，林澈走了過來。\n\n阿達看著他，忽然笑了。\n\n「安靜鬼。」他說，「交給你了。」\n\n「交給我了？」林澈問。\n\n「對啊。」阿達說，「以後，你負責看，我負責在另一個世界……被看。」\n\n他停了停：「不過你放心，我會很想你的。想你的時候，我就去農場摘草莓。」\n\n「那我呢？」林澈說，「我想你的時候，要怎麼辦？」\n\n「你就看鳥啊。」阿達笑，「白頭翁飛過來的樣子，就是我說嗨。」\n\n林澈的眼眶，熱了。\n\n他伸出手。\n\n阿達握住。\n\n「十一點五十九分。」晴晴報時。她的聲音在抖。\n\n「快去！」孩子們大喊。\n\n阿達轉過身，面對鏡子。\n\n鏡子的另一邊，達哥也轉過身。\n\n兩個人，同時伸出手。\n\n同時，踏出一步。\n\n銀霧裡，兩個一模一樣的身影，迎面走來。\n\n一步。兩步。\n\n就在他們擦身而過的瞬間——\n\n兩隻手，在半空中，用力地拍在一起。\n\n啪！\n\n銀白色的光，從掌心炸開，照亮了整座禮堂。\n\n亮得所有人，都閉上了眼睛。\n\n然後，光，慢慢暗下來。\n\n孩子們張開眼睛。\n\n鏡子前，站著一個人。\n\n一模一樣的頭髮，一模一樣的制服，一模一樣的、有點緊張又很勇敢的表情。\n\n是達哥。\n\nB 世界的達哥。\n\n「嗨。」他說，「我來了。」\n\n禮堂裡，安靜了一秒。\n\n然後，阿寶衝上去，抱住了他。\n\n「歡迎你！歡迎你來我們班！」他大哭，「你是我們的達哥了！」\n\n孩子們一擁而上。\n\n而鏡子的另一邊——\n\nB 世界的禮堂裡，阿達站在銀霧前。\n\nB 世界的孩子們，靜靜地看著他。\n\n阿達有點緊張。他抓抓頭，正要開口說點什麼——\n\n「達哥！」B 阿寶第一個喊。\n\n然後，二十六個聲音，一起喊：\n\n「歡迎達哥回家！」\n\n阿達愣在原地。\n\n眼淚，像關不掉的水龍頭，嘩啦嘩啦地掉。\n\n「我……」他哽咽，「我回家了。」\n\n兩邊的禮堂裡，都響起哭聲和笑聲。\n\n林澈站在 A 世界的鏡子前，隔著薄薄的銀霧，看著對面。\n\n對面，B 林澈也站在那裡。\n\n兩個林澈，面對面，中間隔著一面越來越暗的鏡子。\n\n「還有一分鐘。」B 林澈說。他的聲音，從霧裡傳來，輕輕的。\n\n「嗯。」林澈點頭。\n\n「你怕嗎？」B 林澈問。\n\n「本來很怕。」林澈說，「現在不怕了。」\n\n「為什麼？」\n\n「因為我知道，不管鏡子關不關，」林澈笑了，「你都還在。在我這裡。」\n\n他指了指自己的心口。\n\nB 林澈也笑了。他也指了指自己的心口。\n\n「我也是。」\n\n「喂。」林澈忽然說，「最後一句話。」\n\n「說。」\n\n「下次體育課，」林澈說，「記得，你已經跑得很好了。」\n\nB 林澈的眼眶，紅了。\n\n「你也是。」他說，「下次窗邊有鳥飛過的時候，記得跟它揮手。」\n\n兩個少年，隔著一道越來越窄的銀縫，都笑了。\n\n「還有最後一分鐘。」B 林澈說。\n\n「那我們，慢慢說。」林澈說。\n\n鏡子的光，只剩下一道窄窄的縫。\n\n十一點五十九分。\n\n而縫的兩邊，五十二個孩子，都擠了過來。\n\n最後的道別，開始了。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 21 — The Swap\n\n11:58 p.m. Da-ge's words still echoed through the auditorium.\n\n\"Swap?\" A-Da's eyes went wide, looking through the silver mist at the face identical to his own.\n\n\"Swap.\" Da-ge smiled. \"You and I have the same brain. In my world, you'll do even better than me. And in your world, I'll be needed too.\"\n\n\"But...\" A-Da's voice trembled. \"In your world, everyone likes you. Why would you...\"\n\n\"Because,\" Da-ge said, \"I want to know if I can still make people laugh once I've left the applause behind.\"\n\nHe paused: \"And I want to help your world. I want the people there to know that Wu Da's ideas are worth listening to.\"\n\nA-Da's tears fell.\n\n\"You idiot...\" he laughed, tears streaming down. \"You really are... the most handsome me in the whole world.\"\n\nDa-ge laughed loudly: \"Of course! We have the same face!\"\n\nAll the children laughed. And as they laughed, their eyes reddened.\n\n\"Okay.\" A-Da wiped his tears. \"I'll swap with you.\"\n\nHe turned to face his twenty-six World A classmates.\n\n\"Everyone,\" he said. \"I'm leaving.\"\n\nNo one spoke.\n\nA-Da looked at them one by one. Hsiao-Mei, Iron Ox, Tzu-Han, A-Bao...\n\n\"A-Bao.\" He suddenly said. \"From now on, my seat is yours to look after. The marbles in my desk drawer are all yours.\"\n\nA-Bao's eyes instantly reddened.\n\n\"Wh-who wants your marbles!\" he shouted, but his voice shook uncontrollably.\n\n\"And you, Hsiao-Mei.\" A-Da said. \"Next time you cry, remember — the number one joke master A-Da may be gone, but the jokes will stay.\"\n\nHsiao-Mei burst into tears with a loud \"waah.\"\n\n\"A-Da...\" Tzu-Han said quietly. \"I'm sorry. I said your proposal was boring last time...\"\n\n\"Why are you apologizing!\" A-Da laughed. \"You guys! Only now you realize you'll miss me!\"\n\nThe children gathered around.\n\nChing-Ching walked up to him.\n\nThe two of them — one the most serious person in class, the other the loudest.\n\n\"Wu Da,\" Ching-Ching said.\n\n\"What?\" A-Da puffed out his chest. \"Going to scold me? It's your last chance!\"\n\nChing-Ching looked at him. Her eyes were red.\n\n\"I'm sorry,\" she said. \"I always told you to be quiet.\"\n\nA-Da froze.\n\n\"Your ideas were actually really good,\" Ching-Ching said. \"I was in too much of a hurry to keep order, and forgot to listen to you.\"\n\nTears slid down A-Da's face.\n\n\"You...\" his voice choked. \"I've been waiting six years for you to say that.\"\n\nChing-Ching's tears fell too.\n\nIn the dim auditorium, the two of them hugged tightly.\n\nFinally, Lin Che walked over.\n\nA-Da looked at him and suddenly smiled.\n\n\"Quiet ghost,\" he said. \"I'm leaving it to you.\"\n\n\"Leaving what to me?\" Lin Che asked.\n\n\"Everything,\" A-Da said. \"From now on, you take care of the watching. I'll take care of... being watched, in the other world.\"\n\nHe paused: \"But don't worry, I'll miss you a lot. When I miss you, I'll go pick strawberries at the farm.\"\n\n\"Then what about me?\" Lin Che said. \"What do I do when I miss you?\"\n\n\"You watch the birds.\" A-Da grinned. \"The way the white-eyes flies past — that's me saying hi.\"\n\nLin Che's eyes grew hot.\n\nHe held out his hand.\n\nA-Da grasped it.\n\n\"11:59,\" Ching-Ching announced. Her voice trembled.\n\n\"Go, quick!\" the children shouted.\n\nA-Da turned to face the mirror.\n\nOn the other side of the mirror, Da-ge turned too.\n\nThe two of them reached out their hands at the same time.\n\nStepped forward at the same time.\n\nIn the silver mist, two identical figures walked toward each other.\n\nOne step. Two steps.\n\nThe instant they brushed past each other—\n\nTwo hands smacked together in midair.\n\nSmack!\n\nSilvery-white light burst from their palms, illuminating the whole auditorium.\n\nSo bright that everyone shut their eyes.\n\nThen, the light slowly dimmed.\n\nThe children opened their eyes.\n\nIn front of the mirror stood a person.\n\nThe same hair, the same uniform, the same expression — a little nervous, and very brave.\n\nIt was Da-ge.\n\nThe Da-ge of World B.\n\n\"Hi,\" he said. \"I'm here.\"\n\nThe auditorium went quiet for a second.\n\nThen A-Bao charged over and hugged him.\n\n\"Welcome! Welcome to our class!\" he bawled. \"You're our Da-ge now!\"\n\nThe children swarmed over.\n\nAnd on the other side of the mirror—\n\nIn the World B auditorium, A-Da stood before the silver mist.\n\nThe World B children watched him quietly.\n\nA-Da was a little nervous. He scratched his head, about to say something—\n\n\"Da-ge!\" B A-Bao was the first to shout.\n\nThen, twenty-six voices shouted together:\n\n\"Welcome home, Da-ge!\"\n\nA-Da froze where he stood.\n\nTears poured down like a faucet that couldn't be turned off.\n\n\"I...\" he choked. \"I'm home.\"\n\nIn both auditoriums, cries and laughter rang out.\n\nLin Che stood before the World A mirror, looking across through the thin silver mist.\n\nAcross the way, B Lin Che stood there too.\n\nThe two Lin Ches, face to face, separated by a mirror growing dimmer and dimmer.\n\n\"One minute left,\" B Lin Che said. His voice came softly through the mist.\n\n\"Mm.\" Lin Che nodded.\n\n\"Are you scared?\" B Lin Che asked.\n\n\"I was at first,\" Lin Che said. \"But not anymore.\"\n\n\"Why not?\"\n\n\"Because I know that whether the mirror closes or not,\" Lin Che smiled, \"you'll still be here. In here.\"\n\nHe pointed at his chest.\n\nB Lin Che smiled too. He also pointed at his chest.\n\n\"Same here.\"\n\n\"Hey.\" Lin Che suddenly said. \"One last thing.\"\n\n\"Say it.\"\n\n\"Next PE class,\" Lin Che said, \"remember — you already run really well.\"\n\nB Lin Che's eyes reddened.\n\n\"You too,\" he said. \"Next time a bird flies past your window, remember to wave at it.\"\n\nThe two boys, separated by a silver slit growing narrower and narrower, both smiled.\n\n\"One last minute,\" B Lin Che said.\n\n\"Then let's take our time saying it,\" Lin Che said.\n\nThe mirror's light was now only a narrow slit.\n\n11:59 p.m.\n\nAnd on both sides of the slit, all fifty-two children crowded close.\n\nThe final farewell had begun.\n"},{"id":6,"rawContent":"# 第 22 章　最後一分鐘\n\n十一點五十九分。鏡子的縫，只剩一根手指那麼寬。\n\n五十二個孩子，擠在縫的兩邊。\n\n「快快快，最後的道別！」小陽在 B 世界那一邊喊。\n\n晴晴把耳朵湊近縫。\n\nB 晴晴的聲音，從縫裡飄出來：「喂！嚴肅的班長！」\n\n「在！」晴晴喊。\n\n「我們班交給你一個任務！」B 晴晴說。\n\n「說！」\n\n「明天早上，進教室的時候，」B 晴晴的聲音帶笑，「記得笑！」\n\n「收到！」晴晴的眼淚，又掉了下來。可是她真的笑了。\n\n小筠擠到縫邊。\n\n「B 小筠！」她喊。\n\n「我在！」對面的聲音，小小的，卻很清楚。\n\n「我會繼續推理的。」小筠說，「你也要繼續有朋友。」\n\n「你也是。」B 小筠說，「你現在，有二十六個朋友了。」\n\n小筠的眼鏡，又霧了。\n\n安安把臉湊到縫邊：「B 安安！我把畫本，放在抽屜上面了！」\n\n「我也是！」B 安安喊，「我們約好了，畫畫是禮物！」\n\n「畫畫是禮物！」安安喊回去。\n\n阿寶舉著養樂多罐子：「B 阿寶！空罐子我會留著！」\n\n「白癡！要留，也要留滿的！」B 阿寶笑，「下次，帶滿的來！」\n\n「好！」阿寶抹眼淚。\n\n達哥——新的達哥，站在 A 世界這一邊，把臉湊近鏡子。\n\n「喂。」他說。\n\n「喂。」縫的另一邊，阿達的聲音。\n\n兩個交換了世界的吳達，隔著一道光縫，笑了。\n\n「我們成功了。」達哥說。\n\n「我們成功了。」阿達說。\n\n「好好照顧我的世界。」達哥說。\n\n「你也是。好好照顧我的世界。」阿達說。\n\n兩個人，同時把臉貼在鏡面上。涼涼的。\n\n「下次見。」他們同時說。\n\n小陽的聲音，忽然從縫裡炸出來：\n\n「各位——！」\n\n所有人都湊過來。\n\n「最後，我們一起喊一句話！」小陽喊，「我數三二一！」\n\n「三！」\n\n「二！」\n\n「一！」\n\n五十二個聲音，同時響起：\n\n「我們是——平行時空的同班同學！」\n\n聲音穿透了鏡子的縫，穿過兩個世界，在兩座禮堂裡迴盪。\n\n孩子們喊完，都哭了。也都在笑。\n\n林澈和 B 林澈，最後一個，走到鏡子前。\n\n他們同時舉起手，把手掌按在鏡面上。\n\n隔著一層薄薄的、快要消失的銀光，兩隻手，重疊在一起。\n\n「明天見，另一個我。」林澈說。\n\n「明天見。」B 林澈說。\n\n縫，開始合攏。\n\n銀白色的光，一閃，一閃，像心跳。\n\n越來越慢。\n\n越來越慢。\n\n然後，停了。\n\n黑暗。\n\n十二點整。\n\n舊禮堂裡，安靜得連灰塵落下的聲音都聽得見。\n\n孩子們站在原地，誰都沒有動。\n\n鏡子，只是一面鏡子了。蒙著灰，沒有裂痕，沒有光。\n\n「鏡子……」小美的聲音小小的，「關上了。」\n\n沒人回答。\n\n過了很久，阿寶忽然哭出聲。\n\n「我、我還沒說再見……」\n\n「說過了。」晴晴說。她的聲音啞啞的，卻很穩，「我們都說過了。」\n\n「他們會記得嗎？」小美問。\n\n「會。」晴晴點頭，「因為，我們也不會忘。」\n\n達哥走到大家面前。他打開手電筒，照著自己的臉，做了一個鬼臉。\n\n「喂喂喂，」他笑，「你們現在有我在啊。新的笑話，新的點子，新的企劃——」\n\n孩子們看著他，慢慢地，一個一個笑了。\n\n「對啊。」阿寶擦掉眼淚，「我們還有達哥。」\n\n「達哥還在！」孩子們跟著喊。\n\n晴晴走到鏡子前，摸了摸那面老鏡子。\n\n「三十年前，也有人站在這裡。」她輕聲說，「跟我們一樣。」\n\n「他們回家了。我們也該回家了。」\n\n孩子們一個一個站起來，拍了拍身上的灰。\n\n有人還在哭。有人已經開始笑了。\n\n晴晴推開舊禮堂的門。\n\n門外，是九月的夜。海風吹過來，鹹鹹的，涼涼的。\n\n操場後面的空地，安安靜靜的。\n\n那圈溜滑梯的影子，不見了。\n\n孩子們走出禮堂，走進夜色裡。\n\n林澈走在最後面。\n\n他回頭看了一眼。\n\n舊禮堂裡，那面鏡子，靜靜地站在黑暗中。\n\n像一個守了三十年的祕密，終於可以休息了。\n\n「謝謝你。」林澈輕聲說。\n\n他轉身，走進月光裡。\n\n校門口，海聲書店的招牌，在夜裡亮著一盞小小的燈。\n\n藍色的招牌，像一片海。\n\n孩子們經過它，每個人都抬頭看了一眼。\n\n「書店還在耶。」小美說。\n\n「嗯。」晴晴說，「它不會再消失了。」\n\n海風吹過空空的操場。\n\n十二點零五分。\n\n這一天，結束了。\n\n而兩個世界，都還好好的。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 22 — The Final Minute\n\n11:59 p.m. The slit in the mirror was only as wide as a finger.\n\nThe fifty-two children crowded on both sides of the slit.\n\n\"Quick, quick, final goodbyes!\" Xiao-Yang shouted from the World B side.\n\nChing-Ching put her ear close to the slit.\n\nB Ching-Ching's voice floated out from the slit: \"Hey! Serious monitor!\"\n\n\"Here!\" Ching-Ching called.\n\n\"Our class has a mission for you!\" B Ching-Ching said.\n\n\"Say it!\"\n\n\"Tomorrow morning, when you walk into the classroom,\" B Ching-Ching's voice carried a smile, \"remember to smile!\"\n\n\"Mission accepted!\" Ching-Ching's tears fell again. But this time, she really smiled.\n\nHsiao-Yun squeezed up to the slit.\n\n\"B Hsiao-Yun!\" she called.\n\n\"I'm here!\" The voice from the other side was small, but very clear.\n\n\"I'll keep deducing things,\" Hsiao-Yun said. \"You keep having friends.\"\n\n\"You too,\" B Hsiao-Yun said. \"You have twenty-six friends now.\"\n\nHsiao-Yun's glasses fogged up again.\n\nAn-An pressed her face to the slit: \"B An-An! I've put my sketchbook on top of the drawer now!\"\n\n\"Me too!\" B An-An shouted. \"We made a promise — drawing is a gift!\"\n\n\"Drawing is a gift!\" An-An shouted back.\n\nA-Bao held up his Yakult bottle: \"B A-Bao! I'll keep the empty bottle!\"\n\n\"Idiot! If you keep one, keep a full one!\" B A-Bao laughed. \"Next time, bring a full one!\"\n\n\"Deal!\" A-Bao wiped his tears.\n\nDa-ge — the new Da-ge — stood on the World A side and pressed his face near the mirror.\n\n\"Hey,\" he said.\n\n\"Hey.\" From the other side of the slit came A-Da's voice.\n\nThe two Wu Das, who had swapped worlds, smiled through a slit of light.\n\n\"We did it,\" Da-ge said.\n\n\"We did it,\" A-Da said.\n\n\"Take good care of my world,\" Da-ge said.\n\n\"You too. Take good care of my world,\" A-Da said.\n\nThe two of them pressed their faces against the mirror's surface at the same time. It was cool.\n\n\"See you next time,\" they said at the same time.\n\nXiao-Yang's voice suddenly exploded from the slit:\n\n\"Everyone—!\"\n\nEveryone gathered close.\n\n\"For the last time, let's all shout one thing together!\" Xiao-Yang shouted. \"I'll count down!\"\n\n\"Three!\"\n\n\"Two!\"\n\n\"One!\"\n\nFifty-two voices rang out at the same time:\n\n\"We are — classmates from parallel worlds!\"\n\nThe sound pierced through the slit in the mirror, through two worlds, echoing in two auditoriums.\n\nWhen the shouting ended, everyone was crying. And everyone was smiling too.\n\nLin Che and B Lin Che walked up to the mirror last.\n\nThey raised their hands at the same time and pressed their palms against the mirror's surface.\n\nSeparated by a thin, nearly-vanished layer of silver light, the two hands overlapped.\n\n\"See you tomorrow, other me,\" Lin Che said.\n\n\"See you tomorrow,\" B Lin Che said.\n\nThe slit began to close.\n\nThe silvery-white light pulsed, pulsed, like a heartbeat.\n\nSlower and slower.\n\nSlower and slower.\n\nThen, it stopped.\n\nDarkness.\n\nTwelve o'clock sharp.\n\nIn the old auditorium, it was so quiet you could hear the dust settling.\n\nThe children stood where they were. None of them moved.\n\nThe mirror was just a mirror now. Covered in dust, no cracks, no light.\n\n\"The mirror...\" Hsiao-Mei's voice was tiny. \"It's closed.\"\n\nNo one answered.\n\nAfter a long while, A-Bao suddenly burst into tears.\n\n\"I-I never got to say goodbye...\"\n\n\"You did,\" Ching-Ching said. Her voice was hoarse, but steady. \"We all did.\"\n\n\"Will they remember?\" Hsiao-Mei asked.\n\n\"Yes,\" Ching-Ching nodded. \"Because we won't forget either.\"\n\nDa-ge walked up in front of everyone. He clicked on his flashlight, shone it on his face, and made a funny face.\n\n\"Hey, hey, hey,\" he grinned, \"you've got me now. New jokes, new ideas, new proposals—\"\n\nThe children looked at him, and slowly, one by one, they smiled.\n\n\"That's right.\" A-Bao wiped his tears. \"We still have Da-ge.\"\n\n\"Da-ge is still here!\" the children echoed.\n\nChing-Ching walked to the mirror and touched the old glass.\n\n\"Thirty years ago, someone stood here too,\" she said softly. \"Just like us.\"\n\n\"They went home. It's time for us to go home too.\"\n\nThe children stood up one by one and brushed the dust off their clothes.\n\nSome were still crying. Some had already started laughing.\n\nChing-Ching pushed open the old auditorium's door.\n\nOutside was a September night. The sea breeze blew over — salty, cool.\n\nThe empty lot behind the playground was quiet.\n\nThe shadow of the slide was gone.\n\nThe children walked out of the auditorium and into the night.\n\nLin Che walked at the very back.\n\nHe glanced behind him.\n\nInside the old auditorium, the mirror stood silently in the darkness.\n\nLike a secret that had been kept for thirty years, finally allowed to rest.\n\n\"Thank you,\" Lin Che whispered.\n\nHe turned and walked into the moonlight.\n\nAt the school gate, the Haisheng Bookstore sign glowed with a small light in the night.\n\nThe blue sign, like a sea.\n\nThe children passed it, and everyone looked up at it.\n\n\"The bookstore's still here,\" Hsiao-Mei said.\n\n\"Mm.\" Ching-Ching said. \"It won't disappear again.\"\n\nThe sea breeze swept across the empty playground.\n\n12:05 a.m.\n\nThe day had ended.\n\nAnd both worlds were still here, safe and sound.\n"},{"id":7,"rawContent":"# 第 23 章　奇蹟的早晨\n\n九月二十四號，星期一。\n\n太陽照常升起。海聲國小的鐘聲，照常響起。\n\n可是，六年一班的孩子們走進教室的時候，都覺得哪裡不太一樣。\n\n黑板擦得好乾淨。窗戶開著。海風吹進來，把窗簾吹得鼓鼓的。\n\n「早安。」晴晴走進教室。她站在講台上，深吸一口氣。\n\n然後，她笑了。\n\n「早安！」全班嚇了一跳，然後也笑了。\n\n早自習。老師還沒來。\n\n達哥坐在阿達的位置上。他摸摸抽屜——裡面有一顆彈珠。\n\n「阿寶。」達哥小聲說。\n\n「嗯？」阿寶轉過頭。\n\n達哥把彈珠拿出來：「這顆，給你。這是阿達留給你的。」\n\n阿寶接過彈珠，鼻子紅了。\n\n「謝啦。」他說，「我會把它放在書包裡。」\n\n達哥咧嘴一笑，站起來，大聲說：「對了！這星期五，我們來辦個同樂會吧？我有幾個超讚的點子！」\n\n教室裡，安靜了一秒。\n\n達哥心裡一緊。他準備好要被說「安靜」了。\n\n可是，晴晴開口了。她說：「好。你說說看。」\n\n達哥愣住了。\n\n然後，他笑了。笑得眼睛都彎了。\n\n「好咧！」他捲起袖子，「第一，我們要……」\n\n全班都轉過來，聽他說話。\n\n六年一班，第一次，安靜地聽吳達，講完了一整個企劃。\n\n上課鐘響。第一節是數學。\n\n老師在黑板上寫了一道題：「誰會？」\n\n教室裡，舉起了一隻手。\n\n不是達哥。不是小筠。\n\n是林澈。\n\n老師愣了一秒，然後笑著說：「林澈，你說說看。」\n\n林澈站起來。他的聲音不大，可是很清楚。\n\n答對了。\n\n「很好！」老師說。\n\n林澈坐下來。他的心臟，跳得很快。\n\n可是，他笑了。\n\n下課的時候，小筠走到他旁邊。\n\n「你舉手了。」她說。\n\n「嗯。」林澈點頭。\n\n小筠看著他，忽然也笑了：「很好。」\n\n中午，午餐時間。\n\n小筠端著便當，站在座位旁。\n\n她看了看最後一排的角落——她的座位。\n\n然後，她端著便當，走到了中間。\n\n「我可以……坐這裡嗎？」她問。\n\n小美和子涵抬起頭，愣了一下，然後拼命點頭：「可以啊！坐坐坐！」\n\n小筠坐下來，打開便當。\n\n今天，她沒有把便當盒擦得發亮。\n\n因為，她忙著說話。\n\n下午，教室佈置時間。\n\n安安站在佈告欄前，手裡拿著一張畫。\n\n「安安，貼上去啊！」阿寶喊。\n\n「對啊！」達哥喊，「那是你的畫廊！」\n\n安安回頭，看了大家一眼。\n\n然後，她輕輕地，把畫貼了上去。\n\n是那幅海。安靜的、像在嘆氣的海。\n\n「畫得好漂亮。」小美說。\n\n「安安，幫我畫一隻貓！」「幫我畫學校！」\n\n安安笑了：「一個一個來。」\n\n放學後，林澈一個人走到舊禮堂。\n\n鐵門鎖著。他從窗戶看進去。\n\n那面鏡子，靜靜地站在舞台上。\n\n蒙著灰。沒有光。沒有裂痕。\n\n林澈站在窗外，看了很久。\n\n「喂。」他輕聲說，「我做到了。我今天，舉手了。」\n\n鏡子沒有回應。\n\n林澈笑了笑，轉身離開。\n\n就在他走到操場邊的時候，口袋裡的鯨魚貼紙，掉了出來。\n\n他彎腰撿起。\n\n貼紙，變成了灰色。\n\n藍色的小鯨魚，不見了。只剩下一條灰色的、淡淡的輪廓。\n\n林澈愣愣地看著它。\n\n「因為它不屬於這個世界。」一個聲音說。\n\n是晴晴。她不知什麼時候，站在了他身後。\n\n「B 世界的東西，會跟著鏡子一起褪色。」她說，「顏色、溫度……最後，會變成透明的。」\n\n「會消失嗎？」林澈問。\n\n「也許有一天。」晴晴說，「可是，不是今天。」\n\n林澈低頭，看著灰色的鯨魚。\n\n「沒關係。」他把它放回口袋，「在它消失以前，我會記得。」\n\n「記得它是藍色的。記得它是從另一個世界，游過來的。」\n\n晴晴看著他，沒有說話。她從書包裡，拿出一張卡片。\n\n是 B 晴晴的卡片：「嚴肅的班長，也要記得笑。」\n\n卡片的一角，也已經變成了灰色。\n\n「我也會記得。」晴晴說。\n\n兩個孩子，站在操場邊。海風吹過來。\n\n「喂，」晴晴忽然說，「我們去買支鉛筆吧。」\n\n「鉛筆？」\n\n「校門口的書店。」晴晴說，「它開著。」\n\n林澈愣了一下，然後笑了。\n\n「好。」\n\n海聲書店裡，老闆娘笑咪咪的。\n\n「今天要買什麼呀？」\n\n「一支鉛筆。」林澈說。\n\n他挑了一支藍色的。跟他口袋裡那支，一模一樣。\n\n「兩支了。」他自言自語。\n\n走出書店，夕陽把海染成金色。\n\n「明天見。」晴晴說。\n\n「明天見。」林澈說。\n\n回家的路上，林澈忽然停下腳步。\n\n他抬起頭，看向天空。\n\n一隻白頭翁，從榕樹的方向飛過來，繞了一圈，又飛走了。\n\n林澈看著它。\n\n然後，他慢慢地，舉起手，朝它揮了揮。\n\n「嗨。」他說，「阿達。」\n\n海風把這個字，吹向很遠很遠的地方。\n\n而在某個平行世界裡——\n\n一個叫做達哥的男孩，正站在草莓田裡，打了個大大的噴嚏。\n\n「哈啾！」\n\n「怎麼了？」旁邊的同學問。\n\n「不知道。」他抓抓頭，笑了，「總覺得……好像有人在叫我。」\n\n他摘下一顆最紅的草莓，放進口袋裡。\n\n夕陽下，那顆草莓，紅得像一顆小小的太陽。\n\n而兩個世界，都在好好地，過著自己的日子。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 23 — The Morning of Miracles\n\nSeptember 24th, Monday.\n\nThe sun rose as always. The bell at Haisheng Elementary rang as always.\n\nBut when the children of Class 6-1 walked into the classroom, they all felt that something was different.\n\nThe blackboard had been wiped spotless. The windows were open. The sea breeze blew in, puffing the curtains out.\n\n\"Good morning.\" Ching-Ching walked into the classroom. She stood on the podium and took a deep breath.\n\nThen, she smiled.\n\n\"Good morning!\" The whole class jumped, and then smiled too.\n\nMorning self-study. The teacher hadn't arrived yet.\n\nDa-ge sat in A-Da's seat. He felt around the desk drawer — there was a marble inside.\n\n\"A-Bao,\" Da-ge said quietly.\n\n\"Mm?\" A-Bao turned around.\n\nDa-ge took out the marble: \"This one's for you. A-Da left it for you.\"\n\nA-Bao took the marble, his nose reddening.\n\n\"Thanks,\" he said. \"I'll keep it in my backpack.\"\n\nDa-ge grinned, stood up, and said loudly: \"Oh, right! This Friday, let's hold a class party! I've got some awesome ideas!\"\n\nThe classroom went quiet for a second.\n\nDa-ge's heart tightened. He braced himself to be told to \"be quiet.\"\n\nBut Ching-Ching spoke. She said: \"Okay. Tell us about them.\"\n\nDa-ge froze.\n\nThen, he smiled. So wide his eyes curved into crescents.\n\n\"Alright!\" He rolled up his sleeves. \"First, we're going to...\"\n\nThe whole class turned around and listened to him.\n\nClass 6-1, for the first time, quietly listened to Wu Da explain an entire proposal.\n\nThe class bell rang. First period was math.\n\nThe teacher wrote a problem on the blackboard: \"Who can solve this?\"\n\nIn the classroom, a hand went up.\n\nNot Da-ge. Not Hsiao-Yun.\n\nIt was Lin Che.\n\nThe teacher paused for a second, then smiled and said: \"Lin Che, tell us.\"\n\nLin Che stood up. His voice wasn't loud, but it was very clear.\n\nHe got it right.\n\n\"Very good!\" the teacher said.\n\nLin Che sat down. His heart was pounding.\n\nBut he smiled.\n\nAt recess, Hsiao-Yun walked over to him.\n\n\"You raised your hand,\" she said.\n\n\"Mm.\" Lin Che nodded.\n\nHsiao-Yun looked at him, then suddenly smiled too: \"Good.\"\n\nNoon, lunchtime.\n\nHsiao-Yun held her lunch box and stood by her seat.\n\nShe glanced at the corner of the last row — her seat.\n\nThen, carrying her lunch box, she walked to the middle of the classroom.\n\n\"Can I... sit here?\" she asked.\n\nHsiao-Mei and Tzu-Han looked up, froze for a moment, then nodded frantically: \"Of course! Sit, sit, sit!\"\n\nHsiao-Yun sat down and opened her lunch box.\n\nToday, she didn't polish the lunch box until it gleamed.\n\nBecause she was too busy talking.\n\nIn the afternoon, during classroom decoration time.\n\nAn-An stood in front of the bulletin board, holding a drawing in her hands.\n\n\"An-An, put it up!\" A-Bao shouted.\n\n\"Yeah!\" Da-ge shouted. \"It's your gallery!\"\n\nAn-An turned and looked at everyone.\n\nThen, gently, she taped the drawing up.\n\nIt was the sea. The quiet sea, like a sigh.\n\n\"It's so beautiful,\" Hsiao-Mei said.\n\n\"An-An, draw me a cat!\" \"Draw the school for me!\"\n\nAn-An smiled: \"One at a time.\"\n\nAfter school, Lin Che walked alone to the old auditorium.\n\nThe iron gate was locked. He looked in through the window.\n\nThe mirror stood silently on the stage.\n\nCovered in dust. No light. No cracks.\n\nLin Che stood outside the window and looked for a long time.\n\n\"Hey,\" he said softly. \"I did it. I raised my hand today.\"\n\nThe mirror didn't respond.\n\nLin Che smiled a little and turned to leave.\n\nJust as he reached the edge of the playground, the whale sticker in his pocket fell out.\n\nHe bent down and picked it up.\n\nThe sticker had turned gray.\n\nThe little blue whale was gone. Only a faint gray outline remained.\n\nLin Che stared at it blankly.\n\n\"Because it doesn't belong to this world,\" a voice said.\n\nIt was Ching-Ching. She'd somehow appeared behind him.\n\n\"Things from World B fade along with the mirror,\" she said. \"The color, the warmth... in the end, they'll become transparent.\"\n\n\"Will it disappear?\" Lin Che asked.\n\n\"Maybe someday,\" Ching-Ching said. \"But not today.\"\n\nLin Che looked down at the gray whale.\n\n\"It's okay.\" He put it back in his pocket. \"Before it disappears, I'll remember.\"\n\n\"I'll remember it was blue. I'll remember it swam over from another world.\"\n\nChing-Ching looked at him without speaking. She took a card out of her backpack.\n\nIt was B Ching-Ching's card: \"Even a serious monitor should remember to smile.\"\n\nA corner of the card had already turned gray too.\n\n\"I'll remember too,\" Ching-Ching said.\n\nThe two children stood at the edge of the playground. The sea breeze blew over.\n\n\"Hey,\" Ching-Ching suddenly said, \"let's go buy a pencil.\"\n\n\"A pencil?\"\n\n\"The bookstore by the gate,\" Ching-Ching said. \"It's open.\"\n\nLin Che paused for a moment, then smiled.\n\n\"Okay.\"\n\nInside Haisheng Bookstore, the boss lady beamed.\n\n\"What would you like to buy today?\"\n\n\"A pencil,\" Lin Che said.\n\nHe picked a blue one. Exactly the same as the one in his pocket.\n\n\"That makes two,\" he murmured to himself.\n\nOutside the bookstore, the sunset dyed the sea gold.\n\n\"See you tomorrow,\" Ching-Ching said.\n\n\"See you tomorrow,\" Lin Che said.\n\nOn the way home, Lin Che suddenly stopped.\n\nHe looked up at the sky.\n\nA white-eyes bird flew over from the direction of the banyan tree, circled once, and flew off.\n\nLin Che watched it.\n\nThen, slowly, he raised his hand and waved at it.\n\n\"Hi,\" he said. \"A-Da.\"\n\nThe sea breeze carried that word far, far away.\n\nAnd in a certain parallel world—\n\nA boy called Da-ge, standing in a strawberry field, let out a huge sneeze.\n\n\"Achoo!\"\n\n\"What's wrong?\" the classmate beside him asked.\n\n\"I don't know.\" He scratched his head and smiled. \"I just feel... like someone's calling my name.\"\n\nHe picked the reddest strawberry and put it in his pocket.\n\nIn the sunset, that strawberry was red, like a tiny sun.\n\nAnd both worlds were living their own days, well and truly.\n"},{"id":8,"rawContent":"# 第 24 章　平行時空的同班同學（全書大結局）\n\n時間，像海風一樣，輕輕地往前吹。\n\n幾個星期過去了。六年一班，跟以前不太一樣了。\n\n星期五的同樂會，辦成了。達哥的企劃，全班都參與。\n\n會場有氣球、有遊戲、有達哥設計的「猜猜這是哪個世界」攤位。\n\n晴晴負責收錢，笑著說：「這是要蓋溜滑梯的！」\n\n他們要把操場後面的空地，變成一座溜滑梯。\n\n設計圖是安安畫的，預算是小筠算的，宣傳是達哥想的。\n\n林澈負責寫海報。他的字又工整又安靜，每個經過的人，都會停下來看。\n\n同樂會那天，募到好多錢。離溜滑梯，又近了一步。\n\n課堂上，林澈還是會舉手。有時答對，有時答錯。\n\n答錯的時候，他也不害怕了。因為他知道，那沒關係。\n\n小筠的朋友，從三個，變成五個，變成八個。\n\n她還是全班最聰明的人。可是現在，她的聰明，是用來幫大家解謎、算預算、寫邀請卡。\n\n安安的畫，貼滿了半面牆。美術課上，老師對她說了一句話。\n\n「安安，你的畫，像是有光。」\n\n安安笑了。她把這句話，寫在畫本的封面上。\n\n晴晴還是班長。她還是會管秩序。\n\n可是現在，管完秩序，她會補一句：「好了，誰有話要說？」\n\n而達哥，總會第一個舉手。\n\n一切，都在變好。\n\n時間過得很快。轉眼，六月了。\n\n畢業典禮那天，海風特別溫柔。\n\n六年一班的同學們，穿著制服，坐在操場上。\n\n操場後面，有一座嶄新的藍色溜滑梯，閃閃發亮。\n\n低年級的學弟妹們，已經在排隊了。\n\n「我們成功了。」晴晴輕聲說。\n\n「我們成功了。」達哥說。\n\n畢業生代表上台致詞。那個人，是林澈。\n\n他站在台上，看著下面黑壓壓的人群。\n\n他想起體育課的那天。想起那隻舉到一半的手。\n\n他深吸一口氣。\n\n「各位老師、各位同學，大家好。」他開口。\n\n他的聲音不大。可是，很清楚。\n\n台下很安靜。每個人都在聽。\n\n「六年來，我學到了很多事。」他說。\n\n「我學會了算數學、寫作文、跑大隊接力。」\n\n「但是，最重要的是——」\n\n他停了一下，笑了。\n\n「我學會了被看見。也學會了，去看見別人。」\n\n掌聲，像海浪一樣響起來。\n\n林澈看見，晴晴在哭，小筠在笑，安安舉著相機，達哥用力鼓掌。\n\n他忽然想起了另一個人。另一個世界的自己。\n\n「你看到了嗎？」他在心裡說，「我也在發光了。」\n\n畢業典禮結束後，林澈一個人走進舊禮堂。\n\n鐵門沒有鎖。他輕輕推開。\n\n那面鏡子，還站在舞台上。蒙著厚厚的灰。\n\n林澈走到它面前，用袖子，擦掉了一小塊灰。\n\n鏡子裡，映出一個少年。他長高了。肩膀挺了。眼睛裡，有光。\n\n「喂。」林澈說，「我要畢業了。」\n\n鏡子安靜地看著他。\n\n他從口袋裡，拿出那張鯨魚貼紙。\n\n貼紙已經完全透明了，只剩下一圈很淡很淡的輪廓。\n\n他把貼紙，輕輕地貼在鏡框上。\n\n「把鯨魚，放回海裡。」他笑著說。\n\n然後，他整理了一下領子，準備離開。\n\n就在他轉身的瞬間——\n\n鏡面，忽然泛起了一點漣漪。\n\n很淡。很淡。淡得像一陣風，吹過水面。\n\n林澈猛地回頭。\n\n鏡子裡，還是他的倒影。\n\n可是，那圈漣漪裡，浮現出了另一個畫面——\n\n一間教室。一個黑板。一群孩子。\n\n然後，教室裡，舉起了一隻手。\n\n是 B 林澈。\n\n他站起來，回答了一個問題。老師點頭，同學鼓掌。\n\n然後，他轉過頭，朝鏡子的方向，笑了。\n\n那一瞬間，兩個少年，隔著兩個世界，看見了彼此。\n\n「明天見，另一個我。」林澈輕聲說。\n\n漣漪散了。鏡子，又恢復成一塊普通的玻璃。\n\n林澈站了一會，然後，轉身走出禮堂。\n\n門外，陽光亮得刺眼。海風吹過來，帶著海的味道。\n\n操場上，同學們朝他揮手：「林澈！拍照啦！」\n\n「來了！」他笑著跑過去。\n\n畢業照拍完之後，達哥一個人，回到了教室。\n\n他走到自己的座位，打開抽屜——那個原本屬於阿達的抽屜。\n\n裡面，靜靜地躺著一顆草莓。\n\n灰色的。像一顆褪了色的星星。\n\n達哥輕輕地把它拿出來。\n\n他想起那個在鏡子裡，跟他擊掌的少年。\n\n「你這傢伙，」他笑，「連草莓都不吃。」\n\n他走到操場後面，在那座嶄新的溜滑梯旁邊，挖了一個小小的洞。\n\n他把草莓，輕輕地放了進去。蓋上土。\n\n「明年，這裡說不定會長出草莓。」他自言自語，「等它結果了，我再來摘一顆。」\n\n他站起來，拍拍手上的土。\n\n海風吹過溜滑梯，發出輕輕的聲音，像在說「好」。\n\n而在那個平行世界裡——\n\n同樣的六月。同樣的畢業典禮。\n\nB 世界的佈告欄前，站著一個少年。\n\n他看著佈告欄上，那張密密麻麻寫滿字的卡片。\n\n卡片的最後一行寫著：「謝謝你，讓我被看見。」\n\n少年笑了。他伸手，輕輕摸了摸那張卡片。\n\n「不客氣。」他說，「你也讓我被看見了。」\n\n放學的路上，他經過校門口。\n\n那家店，現在是一間 7-ELEVEN。綠色的招牌，在夕陽裡亮著。\n\n他走進去，買了一罐養樂多。\n\n「敬阿寶。」他對著夕陽，輕輕舉了一下罐子。\n\n兩個世界的阿寶，都在某個地方，喝著養樂多。\n\n窗外，白頭翁飛過。\n\n兩個世界。兩個六年一班。\n\n一樣的藍天。一樣的海風。\n\n一樣的、正在長大的孩子們。\n\n他們也許再也見不到面了。\n\n可是，他們永遠是——\n\n平行時空的同班同學。\n\n而故事，會一直記得他們。\n\n就像那面鏡子，記得每一個，照過它的人。\n\n也記得那個黃昏——\n\n一個安靜的男孩，推開舊禮堂的門，看見了另一個自己。\n\n（全書完）\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 24 — Classmates from a Parallel World (The Grand Finale)\n\nTime blew forward gently, like a sea breeze.\n\nA few weeks passed. Class 6-1 was no longer quite the same.\n\nThe Friday party happened. Da-ge's proposal, with the whole class taking part.\n\nThe venue had balloons, games, and a booth Da-ge designed called \"Guess Which World This Is.\"\n\nChing-Ching was in charge of collecting money, saying with a smile: \"This is for building the slide!\"\n\nThey were going to turn the empty lot behind the playground into a slide.\n\nThe blueprint was drawn by An-An, the budget calculated by Hsiao-Yun, and the promotion dreamed up by Da-ge.\n\nLin Che was in charge of the posters. His handwriting was neat and quiet, and everyone who passed by would stop to look.\n\nOn the day of the party, they raised a lot of money. One step closer to the slide.\n\nIn class, Lin Che still raised his hand. Sometimes he got it right, sometimes wrong.\n\nWhen he got it wrong, he wasn't afraid anymore. Because he knew it was okay.\n\nHsiao-Yun's friends went from three, to five, to eight.\n\nShe was still the smartest person in class. But now, her smarts went toward solving puzzles, calculating budgets, and writing invitation cards.\n\nAn-An's drawings covered half a wall. In art class, the teacher said one thing to her.\n\n\"An-An, your drawings seem to have light in them.\"\n\nAn-An smiled. She wrote that sentence on the cover of her sketchbook.\n\nChing-Ching was still the class monitor. She still kept order.\n\nBut now, after keeping order, she would add: \"Alright. Does anyone have something to say?\"\n\nAnd Da-ge would always be the first to raise his hand.\n\nEverything was getting better.\n\nTime passed quickly. In the blink of an eye, it was June.\n\nOn graduation day, the sea breeze was especially gentle.\n\nThe students of Class 6-1, in their uniforms, sat on the playground.\n\nBehind the playground stood a brand-new blue slide, sparkling.\n\nThe younger students were already lining up for it.\n\n\"We did it,\" Ching-Ching said softly.\n\n\"We did it,\" Da-ge said.\n\nThe class representative went up to give the graduation speech. That person was Lin Che.\n\nHe stood on the stage, looking at the sea of people below.\n\nHe thought of that PE class day. He thought of the hand raised halfway.\n\nHe took a deep breath.\n\n\"Dear teachers and fellow students, hello.\" He began.\n\nHis voice wasn't loud. But it was very clear.\n\nThe audience was silent. Everyone was listening.\n\n\"In these six years, I've learned many things,\" he said.\n\n\"I learned math, writing essays, and running the relay.\"\n\n\"But most importantly—\"\n\nHe paused, and smiled.\n\n\"I learned to be seen. And I learned to see others.\"\n\nThe applause rolled in like ocean waves.\n\nLin Che saw Ching-Ching crying, Hsiao-Yun laughing, An-An holding up her camera, and Da-ge clapping hard.\n\nHe suddenly thought of another person. The him in the other world.\n\n\"Did you see it?\" he said in his heart. \"I'm shining now too.\"\n\nAfter the graduation ceremony, Lin Che walked alone into the old auditorium.\n\nThe iron gate wasn't locked. He pushed it open gently.\n\nThe mirror still stood on the stage, covered in thick dust.\n\nLin Che walked up to it and wiped a small patch of dust off with his sleeve.\n\nIn the mirror was reflected a boy. He'd grown taller. His shoulders were straight. There was light in his eyes.\n\n\"Hey,\" Lin Che said. \"I'm graduating.\"\n\nThe mirror watched him silently.\n\nHe took the whale sticker out of his pocket.\n\nThe sticker had gone completely transparent, leaving only a very, very faint outline.\n\nHe gently stuck it onto the mirror's frame.\n\n\"Returning the whale to the sea,\" he said with a smile.\n\nThen he straightened his collar, ready to leave.\n\nThe instant he turned around—\n\nThe mirror's surface suddenly rippled.\n\nVery faint. So faint, like a breeze passing over water.\n\nLin Che whipped his head around.\n\nThe mirror still showed his reflection.\n\nBut inside that ripple, another image surfaced—\n\nA classroom. A blackboard. A group of children.\n\nThen, in that classroom, a hand went up.\n\nIt was B Lin Che.\n\nHe stood up and answered a question. The teacher nodded, and his classmates clapped.\n\nThen, he turned his head and smiled toward the mirror.\n\nIn that moment, two boys, separated by two worlds, saw each other.\n\n\"See you tomorrow, other me,\" Lin Che whispered.\n\nThe ripple faded. The mirror returned to being an ordinary piece of glass.\n\nLin Che stood there for a while, then turned and walked out of the auditorium.\n\nOutside, the sunlight was blindingly bright. The sea breeze carried the smell of the sea.\n\nOn the playground, his classmates waved at him: \"Lin Che! Photo time!\"\n\n\"Coming!\" He smiled and ran over.\n\nAfter the graduation photos, Da-ge returned to the classroom alone.\n\nHe walked to his seat and opened the drawer — the drawer that had once belonged to A-Da.\n\nInside lay a strawberry, quiet and still.\n\nGray. Like a faded star.\n\nDa-ge gently took it out.\n\nHe thought of the boy who'd high-fived him inside the mirror.\n\n\"You...\" he laughed. \"You wouldn't even eat a strawberry.\"\n\nHe walked to the back of the playground, and beside the brand-new slide, he dug a small hole.\n\nHe placed the strawberry inside, gently, and covered it with soil.\n\n\"Next year, maybe strawberries will grow here,\" he murmured to himself. \"When they bear fruit, I'll come pick one.\"\n\nHe stood up and dusted off his hands.\n\nThe sea breeze swept past the slide, making a soft sound, as if saying \"okay.\"\n\nAnd in that parallel world—\n\nThe same June. The same graduation ceremony.\n\nIn front of the World B bulletin board stood a boy.\n\nHe looked at the card on the board, densely packed with handwriting.\n\nThe last line of the card read: \"Thank you for letting me be seen.\"\n\nThe boy smiled. He reached out and gently touched the card.\n\n\"You're welcome,\" he said. \"You let me be seen too.\"\n\nOn the way from school, he passed the school gate.\n\nThe store there was now a 7-ELEVEN. Its green sign glowed in the sunset.\n\nHe walked in and bought a bottle of Yakult.\n\n\"To A-Bao,\" he said, raising the bottle gently toward the sunset.\n\nSomewhere out there, the A-Baos of both worlds were sipping their Yakult.\n\nOutside the window, a white-eyes bird flew past.\n\nTwo worlds. Two Class 6-1s.\n\nThe same blue sky. The same sea breeze.\n\nThe same children, growing up.\n\nThey might never meet again.\n\nBut they will always be—\n\nClassmates from a parallel world.\n\nAnd the story will always remember them.\n\nJust like the mirror remembers everyone who ever looked into it.\n\nAnd it remembers that dusk—\n\nWhen a quiet boy pushed open the door of the old auditorium, and saw another version of himself.\n\n(The End)\n"}];
